window.WIKI = {"entries":{"Artifacts":{"title":"Artifacts","kind":"item","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Heavenly Book","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"First Volume (General Outline), inscribed in the Blood-Dripping Cave of the Abyss of the Undead"},{"t":"p","x":"Second Volume, located in the Ghost King Sect"},{"t":"p","x":"Third Volume, located in the Heavenly Emperor’s Treasury"},{"t":"p","x":"Fourth Volume, located at the Wordless Jade Wall in Tianyin Temple"},{"t":"p","x":"Fifth Volume, within the Ancient Sword of Zhuxian"},{"t":"h","x":"Zhu Xian Ancient Sword","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Owners: Pangu → Qingye Zhenren → Tianchengzi → Daoxuan Zhenren → Zhang Xiaofan"},{"t":"p","x":"Born from the first ray of light in the universe, Pangu wielded the Zhuxian Sword to create the world, only to fall to the earth after exhausting his energy. The sword was discovered by Qingye, the founder of the Qingyun Sect, in the Huanyue Cave 1,300 years ago, and subsequently became the Qingyun Sect's signature sword. Possessing the power to slay gods and immortals, it also has a powerful bloodthirsty aura that can backfire on its wielder. As such, it must be wielded by someone who has reached the Taiqing Realm of the Taiji Xuanqing Dao and possesses a strong and steadfast mind. After Qingye revitalized the Qingyun Sect, he used the Zhuxian Sword to create the Zhuxian Sword Formation and sealed the spiritual energy of Qingyun's seven meridians with the Tianji Seal. Within the Huanyue Cave, the Zhuxian Sword's power increased tenfold."},{"t":"h","x":"Xuanhuo Mirror (Mystic Fire Mirror)","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Owners: Ling Long → Fanxian Valley → Nine-Tailed Heavenly Fox → Six-Tailed Fox → Zhang Xiaofan (Gui Li)"},{"t":"p","x":"The Xuanhuo Mirror (玄火鉴) is an ancient divine artifact from Xiao Ding’s novel Zhu Xian. It originally belonged to the southern witch Linglong, and later became the guardian treasure of Burning Incense Valley. Its appearance is that of a jade-green ring, with a thin plate inlaid at the center bearing a crimson flame totem, and red tassels hanging from both sides. It is classified as a supreme Yang-type magical weapon."},{"t":"p","x":"The Xuanhuo Mirror embodies the essence of ten thousand fires, capable of summoning fire dragons of the Eight Desolations. When combined with the “Eight Fierce Profound Fire Formation” within the Xuanhuo Altar, it can unleash a power strong enough to destroy heaven and earth, and during the War of the Beast God it once burned away his physical body. Its pure Yang energy can suppress the backlash of the Soul-Devouring Staff, as well as subdue the Scarlet Flame Demon Beast and rescue the Nine-Tailed Celestial Fox. The power of this artifact is considered second only to ancient divine relics such as the Zhuxian Sword and the Fulong Cauldron."},{"t":"h","x":"Hehuan Bell","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Owner: Madam Jinling → Biyao"},{"t":"p","x":"The Hehuan Sect's treasure, one of the Demon Cult's four greatest treasures. An open bell, inscribed on its inner wall, its heart delicately intricately crafted, and bound by a thin iron cord. It possesses captivating powers, capable of both attack and defense, rivaling the Zhu Xian Sword."},{"t":"h","x":"Fulong Cauldron","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Owner: ⟦Ghost King|Ghost King⟧"},{"t":"p","x":"The Fulong Cauldron (伏龙鼎), also known as the Dragon-Taming Cauldron or Dragon-Subduing Cauldron, is a magical artifact used to capture and bind the four ancient divine beasts (Huangniao aka. Yellow Bird, Kui Niu, Taotie, dan Zhulong). Completing this process activates the Four Spirits Blood Array (四灵血阵, also called Beast Blood Circle) and unleashes the power of the Asura (修罗, called Wisdom King in the donghua adaptation)."},{"t":"h","x":"Sinister Bead","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Ownder: ⟦Black-Hearted Old Man|Black-Hearted Old Man⟧ > ⟦Master Puzhi|Pu Zhi⟧ > ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧"},{"t":"p","x":"see: ⟦Sinister Bead|Sinister Bead⟧"}]},"Baihu":{"title":"Baihu","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"白虎","gender":"Female","aliases":["Venerable Baihu"],"masters":["Ghost King"],"occupation":["One of the 4 Holy Envoys of the Ghost King sect"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Bai Hu (白虎, literally White Tiger): Formerly a subordinate of Chou Wangyu; the second of the Ghost King Sect's Four Holy Envoys. In the donghua, he is called Venerable Baihu (白虎尊者)."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Baihu-151942.webp"},"Beast Deity":{"title":"Beast Deity","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Beast"],"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Beast Deity (兽神, Shòu Shén), also translated as Beast God, is a central and pivotal character in the xianxia novel Zhu Xian (诛仙). He is the supreme ruler of the ancient and powerful supernatural beasts (yaoshou). Unlike a conventional antagonist, the Beast Deity is a profoundly tragic figure whose existence is defined by love, loneliness, and a search for meaning, making him one of the most complex characters in the narrative."},{"t":"p","x":"Beast Deity is widely recognized as the strongest entity in the world of Zhu Xian."},{"t":"h","x":"Creation and Early Life","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"The Beast Deity was not born but created in ancient times by a supremely powerful Shaman (巫师, Wūshī) of the Li Tribe in the Nanjiang region. To alleviate her profound loneliness, the Shaman gathered the primordial Qi of Slaughter and baleful energy from countless deceased magical beasts across the land. From this concentrated essence of violence and power, she willed a conscious entity into being—the Beast Deity. Thus, he is fundamentally an incarnation of the world's most destructive energies."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationship with Ling Long","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"His nature was initially neutral and naive. His destiny changed when he encountered Ling Long (玲珑), the Shaman's daughter. She was the first human who showed no fear of him and taught him about human language, emotion, love, and compassion. He fell deeply in love with her. To truly be with Ling Long and bridge the gap between his divine beast nature and humanity, the Beast Deity made the ultimate sacrifice: he used his near-limitless power to remodel his spiritual form into a mortal human body of flesh and blood, becoming vulnerable and mortal for love."},{"t":"h","x":"Imprisonment and Resurrection","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"Tragically, Ling Long realized that the Beast Deity's very essence, born from slaughter, would inevitably bring catastrophe to the world. To prevent this and to save him from himself, she performed a powerful ritual, sacrificing her own life to seal him away within the Shaman's Temple in Nanjiang for millennia."},{"t":"p","x":"Thousands of years later, his followers, the Beast Deity cult, aided by Gui Li (the protagonist Zhang Xiaofan after his fall to the demonic path), successfully performed a ritual to break the seal and resurrect him."},{"t":"h","x":"War With Human","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"Upon his return, fueled by grief over Ling Long's loss and resentment towards humanity, the Beast Deity unified the beast hordes and launched a catastrophic war against the human cultivation world. His power was absolute, effortlessly defeating the combined might of the greatest orthodox sects."},{"t":"h","x":"Powers and Abilities","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"Prior to his transformation, the Beast Deity was an immortal entity of pure energy, making him virtually indestructible and the most powerful being in the world. His raw power dwarfed that of any human cultivator."},{"t":"p","x":"Even after becoming mortal, he retained a colossal portion of his power, placing him at the absolute peak of the world's strength. He possessed immense control over the demonic beast horde, could command baleful energy, and his combat prowess was unmatched."}],"ep":53,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Beast_Deity-1a8cfa.jpg","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Beast_Deity_2-5e9657.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Beast_Deity_1-af4d17.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Ep_11-077a00.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Beast_Deity_3-24ee1f.png","cap":""}]},"Bi Yao":{"title":"Bi Yao","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"碧瑶","species":["Human"],"gender":"Female","aliases":["Bi Yao","Holy Empress (In the novel Lù Xiān / 戮仙)"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Bi Yao is one of the female characters in Zhu Xian (Jade Dynasty). She possesses an artifact called the Heartbroken Flower(伤心花) that her mother left to her. It has the ability to neutralize poisons and can also serve as a spiritual weapon. It's the only possession she has left to remind her of her"},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Spunky and bright yet hides her inner fears. Noble and steadfast to her own opinions, instead of following the norms."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Daughter of the Ghost King and lost her mother early on because her father couldn't rescue them in time. She believes her father blames her for the death of her mother since her mother kept her alive in a dark cave, feeding her with her own flesh and blood."},{"t":"p","x":"Because she and her mother were trapped in a cave for so long, it became a deep seeded trauma for her and she is always worried about going hungry."},{"t":"h","x":"Quotes","l":2},{"t":"quote","x":"Is this your way of caring about me?","by":""},{"t":"quote","x":"I'm not suffering. Did you know? The real suffering is actually within our hearts.","by":""},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Zhang Xiaofan","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"She was interested in him at the beginning when she heard that he was from Caomao village and mentioned how he used to play around dark caves. She believed he was the one who threw a few buns down in the cave she was trapped in with her mother."},{"t":"p","x":"Those buns helped her survive long enough before her father found her."},{"t":"h","x":"Ghost King","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"Her father and leader of the Ghost King Sect. She has a complicated relationship with her father, she believes he blames her for her mother's death and wonders if he truly cares about her. Because if he did care for her, then why does he not search for her whenever she leaves the sect? Why does he focus so much of his time on expanding the sect and taking over the other demonic sects?"},{"t":"h","x":"You Ji","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"Her maternal aunt. She knows that her aunt cares for her after her mother left her alone in this world."}],"ep":9,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Biyao_featured-f97f20.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Biyao_featured-6e87cc.png","cap":"1"},{"src":"img/wiki/Biyaox_xiao_fan-eb83cd.png","cap":"Bi Yao x Xiao Fan"}]},"Black-Hearted Old Man":{"title":"Black-Hearted Old Man","kind":"character","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Black-Hearted Old Man, or Heixin Laoren (黑心老人), is a character from the novel Jade Dynasty (Zhu Xian). He was the leader of the Demon Faction's ⟦Blood-Refining Guild|Blood-Refining Hall⟧. Over a thousand years ago, he obtained the world-renowned, extremely malevolent artifact - the \"⟦Sinister Bead|Blood-Sucking Pearl⟧.\" Utilizing its mysterious ability to absorb spirit essence and swallow blood, he refined it into a magical artifact. For a time, he was completely invincible, slaughtering countless righteous figures and achieving immense fame, which subsequently made the Blood-Sucking Pearl one of the Four Treasures of the Demon Faction."},{"t":"p","x":"Under the leadership of the Black-Hearted Old Man, the Blood-Refining Hall once reached the pinnacle of its prosperity, acting as the leading force among the Demon Faction's sects and unifying the Demon Faction. After the death of the Black-Hearted Old Man, the pearl vanished into thin air and its whereabouts remained unknown. His skeletal remains were later discovered inside the Dropping Blood Cave in the Abyss of the Dead Spirit, located within the Ancient Bat Cave on Mount Kongsang, by Zhang Xiaofan (Gui Li), a disciple of Qingyun Sect, one of the three major righteous sects and Bi Yao, the young mistress of the Ghost King Sect, one of the four major sects of the Demon Faction. Out of anger that her magical artifact, the Sad Flower, had been blackened by ancient corpse poison, Bi Yao shattered his bones, but Zhang Xiaofan subsequently gathered and reassembled the broken remains."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[]},"Blood-Refining Guild":{"title":"Blood-Refining Guild","kind":"faction","facts":{"type":"Demonic","aliases":["Blood Refining Hall"],"status":"Inactive","founder":["⟦Heixin Lao Ren|Heixin Lao Ren⟧"],"members":["⟦Ye Gou|Ye Gou⟧","⟦Lin Feng|Lin Feng⟧","⟦Xiao Zhou|Xiao Zhou⟧","⟦Mei Miao|Mei Miao⟧"],"enemies":["⟦Qingyun Sect|Qingyun Sect⟧ ⟦Tian Yin Temple|Tian Yin Temple⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Also Known as Blood Refining Hall"},{"t":"h","x":"Description","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Pronounciation: Lian Xie Tang - 炼血堂"},{"t":"p","x":"One of the demonic cults that specializes in spells and skills involved with blood. Some of the members can drain blood from their enemies and use it to become stronger."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"The founder of the Blood-Refining Guild, ⟦Black-Hearted Old Man|Heixin Laoren⟧, was the original owner of the sinister bead that came to Zhang Xiaofan's possession."},{"t":"h","x":"Notable Members","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Nian Lao Da|Nian Laoda⟧ (年老大): Ninth level of the First Realm. A burly man with a full beard. The leader of the Blood Refining Hall. He possesses the Crimson Demon Eye and Blackheart Token."],[1,"Lin Feng (林锋): Ninth level of the First Realm. A young man dressed in white. A relative of the Wind Moon Ancestor. He possesses the Mountain and River Fan."],[1,"\"Meimao Shaofu\" (美貌少妇): “Meimao” is not her real name; it is simply a descriptive term, and her real name remains unknown. She possesses the Immortal-Binding Rope."],[1,"⟦Ye Gou|Ye Gou Daoren / Taoist YeGou⟧ (野狗道人): Tall and lanky, with drooping eyelids, a prominent nose, upward-pointing ears, crimson-red lips, and a long tongue that occasionally sticks out of his mouth. He is loyal to the Blood Refining Hall and has feelings for Zhou Xiaohuan. He wields the Gray Fang Club."],[1,"Liu Gao (刘镐): A tall, thin man. He possesses a yellow flying sword."],[1,"⟦Xiao Zhou|Xiao Zhou⟧ (小周): An alias used by ⟦Xiao Yicai|Xiao Yicai⟧ of Qingyun Sect while he was working undercover in the Blood Refining Hall."]]}]},"Cang Song":{"title":"Cang Song","kind":"character","facts":{"titles":["Head of Dragon Peak"]},"blocks":[],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Cangsong-f855fd.png"},"Chou Wangyu":{"title":"Chou Wangyu","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"仇忘语","gender":"Male","occupation":["Leader of the Demon Cult (previous generation)"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Chou Wangyu (Chinese: 仇忘语; pinyin: Chóu Wàngyǔ) is a male character in the novel Zhu Xian (English: Jade Dynasty). He is the previous generation leader of the Demon Cult (魔教; also called the Holy Cult, 圣教) and appears primarily in the official prequel Zhu Xian: Barren Expedition (诛仙前传：蛮荒行), as well as in background history of the main novel."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Chou Wangyu is described as a once-in-generations prodigy of the Demon Cult. According to later accounts, he rose from obscurity as an unknown disciple of the Longevity Hall (长生堂). After entering the Nether Abyss (冥渊) at the Barren Wilderness Sacred Hall (蛮荒圣殿), he obtained the Demon Cult's supreme scripture, the Heavenly Demon Strategy (天魔策), and cultivated the sinister art known as Profound Yin Ghost Qi (玄阴鬼气)."},{"t":"p","x":"Within about twenty years he unified most of the long-fragmented Demon Cult factions and became cult leader. His personal treasure was the Heavenly Demon Banner (天魔幡 / 天魔蟠)."},{"t":"h","x":"History: Attack on Qingyun and death","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"About a century before the main events of Zhu Xian, Chou Wangyu led a full-scale assault on Qingyun Sect, intending to replace it as the dominant power of the cultivation world. In that war he successively defeated or forced back several leading Qingyun figures, including sect leader Tianchengzi, Wan Jianyi, Zhenyu, and the sacred beast Water Qilin."},{"t":"p","x":"The tide turned when Tianchengzi activated the Zhu Xian Sword Formation (诛仙剑阵) with the ancient Zhu Xian Sword. Chou Wangyu was mortally wounded by the sword's killing aura, which even techniques recorded in the Heavenly Demon Strategy could not fully suppress."},{"t":"p","x":"On his deathbed he accepted responsibility for the defeat, ordered his remains cremated and his ashes scattered beneath the Asura Tower of the Barren Wilderness Sacred Hall, and commanded Qinglong to withdraw the cult to the wilderness and not re-enter the Central Plains for sixty years. After his death the Demon Cult fractured again. The later Ghost King (Wan Renwang), father of Bi Yao, belonged to that subsequent generation."},{"t":"h","x":"Associates","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Qinglong (青龙) — first of the Four Holy Envoys and Chou Wangyu's closest confidant."],[1,"Baihu (白虎), You Ji / Zhuque (幽姬 / 朱雀), and Xuanwu (玄武) — originally his subordinates among the Four Holy Envoys."]]}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[]},"Dahuang":{"title":"Dahuang","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Dahuang (大黄) is a character in \"Zhu Xian\" and its sequel. Originally, he was a yellow dog raised by ⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧, the head of Dazhu Peak of Qingyun Sect. Later, he became the loyal companion of the protagonist ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ (Gui Li) and continued to accompany his son ⟦Zhang Xiaoding|Zhang Xiaoding⟧ in \"Zhu Xian II\".The character is known as the \"enlightened old dog,\" and appears throughout the original trilogy, forming an emotional bond connecting the two generations of protagonists."}]},"Dao Xuan":{"title":"Dao Xuan","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"道玄","species":["Human"],"gender":"Male","titles":["Sect Leader of Qingyun Sect, Head of Heavenly Peak"],"aliases":["Dao Xuan"],"masters":["Tian Chengzi (the 17th generation leader of the Qingyun Sect)"],"disciples":["⟦Xiao Yicai|Xiao Yicai⟧"],"occupation":["Sect Leader of Qingyun Sect","Head of Tongtian Peak"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Dao Xuan, respectfully addressed as \"Dao Xuan Zhenren\", is a male character in the novel Zhu Xian."},{"t":"p","x":"He was the 18th-generation sect leader of the Qingyun Sect and also the seventh-generation head of the main branch, Tongtian Peak."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Wears a Dark Green Daoist Robe, possessing an immortal-like demeanor and crane-like bone structure, with gentle, bright eyes, a long beard reaching his chest, and a refined, ancient countenance."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Profoundly thoughtful and calculating, deeply devoted to his sect, righteous and awe-inspiring, and compassionate towards all living beings."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"His mastery of the Dao was profound and unfathomable. He was deep-thinking, extremely shrewd, deeply devoted to his sect, righteous and awe-inspiring, and compassionate towards all living beings. He shared a bond as close as brothers with his junior fellow disciple, ⟦Wan Jianyi|Wan Jianyi⟧ ."},{"t":"p","x":"For the sake of his sect and the common people of the world, Dao Xuan did not hesitate to risk using the Zhu Xian Sword - The First Divine Sword in the Novel Zhu Xian Formation twice. The first was during the Righteous-Demonic War, and the second was during the Beast God Calamity."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"During the battle against the ⟦Beast Deity|Beast God⟧, he forced the use of the Zhuxian Sword Formation and forcibly activated the Heavenly Mechanism Seal. As a result, he was backlashed by the deeply malevolent spirit of the Zhuxian Sword. Ultimately, his mind was deluded by the sword's spirit, and he unfortunately fell into demonic ways, which led him to cultivate the Profound Yin Ghost Qi and kill ⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧ ."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Daoxuan-d91a85.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/DaoYun_2-0c84a3.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Daoyun-a9ee32.png","cap":""}]},"Daoist Qingye":{"title":"Daoist Qingye","kind":"character","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Master Qing Ye (青叶真人, Qingye Zhenren) is a character in the novel Zhu Xian (also known as Jade Dynasty)."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He was the 11th Sect Leader of the ⟦Qingyun Sect|Qingyun Sect⟧. Originally a poor scholar who was exceptionally talented yet failed the imperial examinations repeatedly, he did not join the Qingyun Sect until the age of 22, when he was accepted as the last personal disciple by ⟦Wu Fangzi|Wu Fangzi⟧, the 11th Sect Leader of Qingyun."},{"t":"p","x":"After only two years of cultivation, Master Qing Ye’s strength rivaled that of his master, Wu Fangzi. Granted an ancient scroll, he went into secluded meditation inside the ⟦Huanyue Cave|Huanyue Cave⟧ for 13 years. When he emerged, his breakthrough triggered extraordinary natural phenomena, signaling that his mastery of the Daoist arts had reached a divine realm."},{"t":"p","x":"Upon succeeding as Sect Leader, Master Qing Ye reformed the sect's rules, re-forged the broken ⟦Zhu Xian Sword|Zhuxian Sword⟧, and created the \"One Qi Transforms into Three Pure Ones\" technique, hiding its secret within the blade. He subdued the spiritual beast ⟦Water Qilin|Water Qilin⟧ to guard the mountain gates and established the ⟦Zhuxian Sword Formation|Zhuxian Sword Formation⟧, which secured the Qingyun Sect's position as the pillar of the Righteous Path for a thousand years."},{"t":"p","x":"Wielding the Zhuxian Sword, his power awed the entire world, commanding respect from both righteous immortals and demonic practitioners alike. Before passing away at the end of his lifespan, he took on only seven disciples to govern the seven peaks, laying a thousand-year foundation for Qingyun's prosperity."},{"t":"p","x":"Master Qing Ye's legendary cultivation journey and the Zhuxian Sword Formation are still praised throughout the cultivation world today. With his absolute strength, he restored a fading sect to its peak, earning him the title of the Ancestor of Restoration of the Qingyun Sect."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[]},"Donghua":{"title":"Donghua","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"English Title: Jade Dynasty"},{"t":"h","x":"Season 1","l":2},{"t":"table","rows":[["Aired:","Aug 2, 2022 to Jan 17, 2023"],["Status:","Finished Airing"]]},{"t":"quote","x":"What is good and what is evil?","by":""},{"t":"table","rows":[["Ep #","Release Date","Summary"],["Ep 1","","Young ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ and young ⟦Lin Jingyu|Lin Jingyu⟧ were having another spar within Caomiao village and they end up at an isolate temple where ⟦Master Puzhi|Master Puzhi⟧ was resting. They didn't realize that someone was going after this Master and Zhang Xiaofan ends up with an artifact called the sinister bead in his possession. Everyone else gets massacred overnight and the two children get taken in by Qingyun Sect."],["Ep 2","",""],["Ep 3","",""]]},{"t":"h","x":"Season 2","l":2},{"t":"table","rows":[["Aired:","Mar 30, 2024"],["Status:","Finished Airing"],["Production Company:","Tencent Penguin Pictures"],["Network:","Tencent Video"],["Studio:","Cloud Art"],["Country:","China"],["Total Episode:","26"]]},{"t":"table","rows":[["Ep #","Release Date","Summary"],["Episode 1","",""],["Episode 2","",""],["Episode 3","",""]]},{"t":"h","x":"Season 3","l":2},{"t":"table","rows":[["Aired:","Jun 12, 2025"],["Status:","Finished Airing"],["Production Company:","Tencent Penguin Pictures"],["Network:","Tencent Video"],["Total Episodes:","26"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Season 4 (finale)","l":2},{"t":"table","rows":[["Aired:","August 21, 2026"],["Status:","Currently airing"],["Production Company:","Tencent Penguin Pictures"],["Network:","Tencent Video"],["Total Episodes:","26"]]}],"img":"img/wiki/ZhuXian_S1-d27051.jpg","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/ZhuXian_S1-bd334e.jpg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/ZhuXian_S2-6c7d94.jpeg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Jade_dynasty_season_3_poster-2f2ce1.jpg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Season4-jadedynasty-799b52.jpg","cap":""}]},"Eight Fiends Formation":{"title":"Eight Fiends Formation","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Eight Ferocious Deities Fire Array or Eight Fiends Formation (八凶玄火法阵) is handed down by the ancient Shaman God, this array must be summoned using the Incense Valley's inherited treasure, the Flame Dragon Ring (Xuan Huo Jian / ⟦Artifacts|Mystic Fire Mirror⟧), and is powered by centuries of accumulated volcanic spiritual energy. It can summon the \"Crimson Flame Demon Beast,\" the guardian beast of the array. The greater the power of the mystical fire within the formation, the more formidable the Crimson Flame Demon Beast becomes. When combined with the incantations of the Southern Border Shaman Tribe, it can even summon the terrifying legendary beast capable of destroying all creation—the ultimate summoned entity of the Eight Ferocious Deities Fire Array, the \"Eight-Desolation Fire Dragon.\" Burning everything in existence, it possesses the wondrous power to shatter heaven and earth."},{"t":"p","x":"Alternative names:"},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"八凶玄火法阵"],[1,"Baxiong Xuanhuo formation"],[1,"The Eight Ferocious Deities Fire Array"],[1,"Eight Fierce Profound Fire Formation"],[1,"Eight Ferocious Flame Array"],[1,"Eight Fierce Mystic Fire Formation"],[1,"Eight Fiend Xuanhuo Formation"],[1,"Eight Fiends Mysterious Fire Formation"],[1,"Eight Fiends Formation"]]}]},"Fa Shan":{"title":"Fa Shan","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/FaShan-0c978f.png"},"Fa Xiang":{"title":"Fa Xiang","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"法相","gender":"Male"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Faxiang is a male character in the novel Jade Dynasty."},{"t":"p","x":"Fa Xiang's characteristics and storyline differ across the drama, novel, manhua, and donghua versions."},{"t":"p","x":"In the drama adaptation, he is not a monk and is in a romantic relationship with a woman named Ding Ling, an original character created for the TV series (a subordinate of Jin Ping'er of the Hehuan Sect )."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He has a playful and exuberant personality with exaggerated expressions, serving as the comic relief in the series."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Faxiang is a disciple of the Tianyin Pavilion, with Puhong as his master, and his magical artifact is the Samsara Pearl."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/FaXiang-e494c2.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Fa_Xiang_golden_body_2-b0a399.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Fa_Xiang_perfil-6336ba.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Fa_Xiang-961a01.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Faxiang_2x2-29d9e7.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Faxiang-fec860.png","cap":""}]},"Fen Xiang Valley":{"title":"Fen Xiang Valley","kind":"faction","facts":{"zh":"焚香谷","type":"Righteous","status":"Active","members":["⟦Li Xun|Li Xun⟧","⟦Yan Hong|Yan Hong⟧"],"allies":["⟦Qingyun Sect|Qingyun Sect⟧","⟦Tian Yin Temple|Tian Yin Temple⟧"],"enemies":["⟦Ghost King Sect|Ghost King Sect⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"also known as the Burning Incense Valley."},{"t":"h","x":"Description","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Pronounciation: Fen Xiang Gu - 焚香谷"},{"t":"p","x":"Burning Incense Valley (Fenxiang Valley) is one of the three major righteous sects in Xiao Ding's novel Zhu Xian, alongside Qingyun Sect and Tianyin Temple. It is located in a volcanic valley in the southern borderlands, adjacent to the Ten Thousand Great Mountains, where it guards a major route connecting the Central Plains with the territories of other races. For a thousand years, the sect has defended against invasions by evil forces by combining the witchcraft of the ancient Wu people with orthodox Taoist techniques."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Its history can be traced back 1,500 years, when the sect's founding patriarch discovered secret witchcraft techniques at the ancient Wu ruins known as the Black Fire Altar (玄火坛) in the southern borderlands and established the sect. Fanxiang Valley specializes in fire-based techniques and possesses its most powerful protective formation, the Eight Fiends Mysterious Fire Formation (八凶玄火法阵). In the past, using the ⟦Artifacts|Mysterious Fire Mirror⟧ (玄火鉴), the sect summoned the Eight Desolate Fire Dragon (八荒火龙) to intimidate and repel demon beasts. The local people revered the sect as gods."},{"t":"h","x":"Trivia","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"The sect’s headquarters were located in a volcanic region characterized by lava terrain."}]},"Fulong Cauldron":{"title":"Fulong Cauldron","kind":"item","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Fulong Cauldron (伏龙鼎), also known as the Dragon-Taming Cauldron or Dragon-Subduing Cauldron, is the ancestral treasure of the ⟦Ghost King Sect|Ghost King Sect⟧. it is a magical artifact used to capture and bind the four ancient divine beasts (Huangniao aka. Yellow Bird, Kui Niu, Taotie, dan Zhulong). Completing this process activates the Four Spirits Blood Array (四灵血阵, also called Beast Blood Circle) and unleashes the power of the Asura (修罗, called Wisdom King in the donghua adaptation)."}]},"Ghost King":{"title":"Ghost King","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male","titles":["Head of Ghost King Sect"],"aliases":["鬼王 (Gui Wang) Wan Ren Wang"],"spouse":["⟦Xiao Chi|Xiao Chi⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Ghost King is the sect master of the Ghost King Sect within the Demon Sect in the novel Zhu Xian. He operates under the alias Wan Renwang and is the father of ⟦Bi Yao|Bi Yao⟧."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Resembles a middle-aged scholar. He has slender eyebrows, a square face, elegant features, piercing eyes, and a full forehead, exuding an imposing aura of dignity within his scholarly demeanor."},{"t":"p","x":"He wears a scholar's robe with a pale purple jade pendant hanging from his waist, which is exquisitely carved and faintly radiates an auspicious aura."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"An ambitious and formidable figure in the Demon Sect. The Ghost King is skilled in strategy and schemes."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"As a 42nd-generation disciple of the Demon Sect and the leader of one of the four major demonic factions, he aims to restore the Demon Sect to the glory it enjoyed during the era of the Black Heart Elder. He once schemed to induce Zhang Xiaofan to defect from the Qingyun Sect and join the Ghost King Sect."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Bi Yao","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"The only daughter of the Ghost King and Xiao Chi , whom the Ghost King doted on immensely."}],"ep":14,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/GhostKingS2-399fa8.png"},"Ghost King sect":{"title":"Ghost King sect","kind":"faction","facts":{"zh":"鬼王宗","members":["⟦Bi Yao|Bi Yao⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Description","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Pronounciation: Gui Wang Zong - 鬼王宗"},{"t":"p","x":"An ambitious sect that seeks to unite all of the demonic sects."}]},"HeHuan Sect":{"title":"HeHuan Sect","kind":"faction","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The He Huan Sect (合欢派, Hē Huān Pài) is one of the four major demonic sects in the novel Zhu Xian (诛仙), also known as Jade Dynasty. While the righteous sects, like the Qing Yun Sect, practice cultivation focused on morality and spiritual enlightenment, the demonic sects pursue power through other, often unorthodox, means."},{"t":"p","x":"The He Huan Sect, in particular, is known for its cultivation methods that are rooted in emotional and sensual power, often involving the use of feelings and relationships to enhance their abilities. This makes them distinct from the other demonic sects which might focus more on brute force, blood arts, or other dark practices. The members were infamous for its cultivation practices that harness dual cultivation, charm, desire, and emotional manipulation to advance spiritually; its members are often seductive, cunning, and psychologically dangerous, using pleasure and deception as weapons rather than relying solely on brute force."},{"t":"p","x":"A key figure associated with the He Huan Sect is Jin Ping'er (金瓶儿). She is a disciple of the sect and is known for her beauty and cunning nature. While her allegiance is to her sect, her path often intersects with the protagonist, Zhang Xiaofan, and the righteous sects, leading to complex and sometimes conflicting relationships."}]},"Heaven nine tailed fox":{"title":"Heaven nine tailed fox","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[]},"Heavenly Books":{"title":"Heavenly Books","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Heavenly Book (天书) is a mystical tome from the novel Zhu Xian and its derivative works. It consists of five volumes."},{"t":"p","x":"The Heavenly Book originated as a manifestation of the laws of Heaven and Earth at the beginning of creation. Its central principle is “Heaven and Earth are not benevolent; they regard all things as straw dogs.” It records the natural laws governing phenomena such as the changes of yin and yang and the interactions of the five elements, and is regarded as the common source of the cultivation techniques of both the righteous and demonic paths. Cultivators from different schools who comprehend the same volume of the Heavenly Book can derive Buddhist, Daoist, and demonic cultivation techniques from it. For example, the founder of Tianyin Temple comprehended Great Brahma Prajna from the Wordless Jade Wall, while an ancient predecessor of the Qingyun Sect comprehended the Taiji Xuanqing Dao from an unnamed ancient scripture."},{"t":"p","x":"The First Volume of the Heavenly Book was first discovered inside a golden chest in a stone chamber within the Dripping Blood Cave. Zhang Xiaofan and Lu Xueqi obtained the volume while exploring the cave. The Demonic Cult has passed down four volumes of the Heavenly Book since ancient times, but most of them have been lost, while legends of the fifth volume have continued to circulate throughout the cultivation world."},{"t":"p","x":"The Heavenly Book was not created by mortals. It embodies the central principle that “Heaven and Earth are not benevolent; they regard all things as straw dogs” and explains the laws governing yin and yang, the five elements, and other natural phenomena. Depending on the cultivator's disposition and understanding, its teachings can give rise to Buddhist, Daoist, or demonic cultivation techniques."},{"t":"h","x":"Locations of the Heavenly Book Volumes","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"First Volume (General Outline), inscribed in the Blood-Dripping Cave of the Abyss of the Undead"],[1,"Second Volume, located in the Ghost King Sect"],[1,"Third Volume, located in the Heavenly Emperor’s Treasury"],[1,"Fourth Volume, located at the Wordless Jade Wall in Tianyin Temple"],[1,"Fifth Volume, within the Ancient Sword of Zhuxian"]]}]},"Hei Hu":{"title":"Hei Hu","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male","masters":["⟦Ling Long|Ling Long⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Heihu (黑虎, literally 'Black Tiger') is one of the ⟦Seven Warriors|Seven Warriors⟧ under ⟦Ling Long|Linglong⟧, and an evil spirit. He holds a giant sword in his right hand and a massive shield in his left. He is the elder brother of ⟦Heimu|Heimu⟧."},{"t":"p","x":"Originally a human, he became an evil spirit after death, tasked with guarding sacred sites like the Secret Cave in the Southern Border and the area surrounding the ⟦Beast Deity|Beast God⟧."}],"ep":53,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/HeiHu-abc2cd.webp"},"Hei Mu":{"title":"Hei Mu","kind":"character","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Hei Mu (黑木, literally Blackwood): One of the Seven Warriors serving ⟦Ling Long|Linglong⟧. He is a lich and a subordinate of the ⟦Beast Deity|Beast God⟧, as well as an old friend of ⟦Shang Guan Ce|Shangguan Ce⟧. He possesses the Black Fire Essence Pearl (黑火精珠)."}],"ep":45,"ch":null,"tags":[]},"Huanyue Cave":{"title":"Huanyue Cave","kind":"place","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Huanyue Cave (幻月洞府, literally Illusion Moon Cave) is an ancient secret realm and core restricted area of the Qingyun Sect in the novel Zhu Xian. It is located deep within the rear mountains of Tongtian Peak and has traditionally been accessible only to the sect's leaders."},{"t":"p","x":"It is both a historic sacred site where ⟦Daoist Qingye|Daoist Qingye⟧ secluded himself for twelve years to comprehend the Unnamed Ancient Scripture and restore the Qingyun Sect to prominence, as well as a mysterious place where the Ancient ⟦Zhu Xian Sword|Zhuxian Sword⟧ was sealed. The cave was named after the fantastical scenery created by strange rocks under the moonlight. It can only be opened by activating a Taiji diagram mechanism using the power of the Shangqing Realm, while intruders who enter it are subjected to illusions that test their state of mind. Its interior layout incorporates the principles of Qimen Dunjia, with the central hall connected radially to eight gates. As a key setting in the novel, ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ (Gui Li) entered the cave twice. He ultimately confronted his inner demons and overcame his attachments within the illusions, fused the cultivation techniques of the Buddhist, Daoist, and Demonic paths, and comprehended the true meaning of the Fifth Volume of the Heavenly Book, completing his transformation from an avenger into a protector."},{"t":"p","x":"According to legend, ⟦Qingyunzi|Qingyunzi⟧, the founding patriarch of the Qingyun Sect, once obtained the Unnamed Ancient Scripture within the cave and, after years of arduous cultivation, established the sect. Later, Qingye Daoist comprehended profound abilities there and obtained the Ancient Zhuxian Sword, enabling the Qingyun Sect to become the leader of the righteous path."}]},"Jade Dynasty The Movie: Ten Years on Different Paths":{"title":"Jade Dynasty The Movie: Ten Years on Different Paths","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Jade Dynasty The Movie: Ten Years on Different Paths (诛仙剧场版 十年殊途) is the upcoming animated theatrical special based on Jade Dynasty (Zhu Xian). It is being produced by Yuntu Animation and Tencent Video, the same production team behind the main Jade Dynasty donghua series. The project was officially announced at the 2025 Tencent Video Animation Awards and is planned for release in 2026."},{"t":"p","x":"The movie focuses on Zhang Xiaofan and his identity as Gui Li, exploring the decade-long struggle between his past as Zhang Xiaofan and his life as Gui Li. Its official promotional tagline describes Zhang Xiaofan as someone whose fate has become intertwined and who must break through his lingering obsession and move forward against the current. The official 2026 promotional material further emphasizes this dual identity with the line, “He is Gui Li, and also Zhang Xiaofan.”"},{"t":"p","x":"Unlike a regular season of the donghua, Ten Years on Different Paths is a standalone animated movie/special connected to the main Jade Dynasty storyline. Current information describes it as a Tencent Video-exclusive production, rather than a conventional cinema release. Despite the Chinese title using 剧场版 (theatrical version), the film is scheduled to be released online via Tencent Video rather than in theaters."}],"img":"img/wiki/Jade_dynasty_the_movie-99c4ea.jpg"},"Jin Ping'er":{"title":"Jin Ping'er","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Female","aliases":["金瓶儿","Young Master of Charm"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Jin Ping'er is one of the Three Young Masters of the Demon Sect known as the Wonderful Young Master."},{"t":"p","x":"She is a disciple of San Miao Xianzi, the leader of the Hehuan Sect, and an outstanding member of the sect. Often dressed in pale yellow garments, she is skilled in the Charm Heart Art and is known as the \"Wonderful Young Master.\""},{"t":"p","x":"She, along with ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Gui Li⟧ (the Blood Young Master) of the Ghost King Sect and ⟦Qin Wuyan|Qin Wuyan⟧ (the Poison Young Master) of the Wandu Sect, are collectively known as the Three Young Masters of the Demon Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"She was once saved from a severe injury by ⟦Xiao Huan|Xiao Huan⟧ using the Soul Retrieval Art, and since then, the two have been as close as sisters. Beautiful, charming, and captivating, she possesses a strong inner will, is clever and cunning, and would resort to any means necessary for survival. She is adept at using the Charm Heart Art to bewitch others but has never fallen in love with any man. She once harbored a faint, ambiguous affection for the male protagonist, ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧, and dislikes Zhang Xiaofan's pet, ⟦Xiao Hui|Xiao Hui⟧. After being saved by Xiao Huan's miraculous Soul Retrieval Art, she becomes as close as sisters with Xiao Huan in the story. At the end of the book, she wanders the world together with Zhou Yixian , Xiao Huan, and Wild Dog Taoist."},{"t":"p","x":"In Jade Dynasty II, she joins the remnants of the Demon Sect, the \"Yinmo Sect,\" led by Qin Wuyan, and serves as its deputy leader. The text reveals that she wants Qin to help her find the ultimate yang treasure, the \"Fire Phoenix Flame Jade,\" to suppress the yin energy within her body. Her subordinates include the squad led by Xu Menghong, in which the protagonist Wang Zongjing is undercover."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She was a beautiful woman dressed entirely in goose-yellow robes, her eyes brimming with emotion, a faint smile playing at the corners of her lips, her dark hair cascading gently over her shoulders. Her gaze was watery and deep; a single glance seemed enough to make one lose themselves in it, never wishing to surface again."},{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Yicai glanced at her and saw her bright eyes were like clear water, sparkling and luminous. Seen in the dim light of dusk, they shone like stars in the night sky, truly enough to make one's heart flutter."}],"ep":21,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/JinPingerSeason4-eb52c2.webp","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Jin_Ping_er-e083e0.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Jin_Ping_er_3-3013ab.png","cap":""}]},"Li Xun":{"title":"Li Xun","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male","aliases":["李洵 (Li Xun)"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Li Xun is a character in the novel Zhu Xian and its sequel, Zhu Xian II ."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"At first appearance, he was said to have a handsome face."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Extremely arrogant and haughty, to the point of looking down on everyone. As soon as he encountered members of the Qingyun Sect , he wanted to duel with them."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is the head disciple of the Burning Incense Valley, a student of Valley Master Yun Yilan, and wields the magical artifact Nine Yang Ruler. Alongside his junior sister Yan Hong , he is known as one of the \"Twin Heroes of Burning Incense Valley\" and is designated as the next successor to the Valley Master position. His mother is the eldest daughter of the City Lord of Yuzhou, making him a cousin to the Qingyun Sect 's Zeng Shushu , though they have been at odds since childhood due to his arrogant personality."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Li Xun first appears at the Ancient Cave of Ten Thousand Bats, immediately displaying an arrogant attitude and clashing with disciples from the Qingyun Sect . Over a span of ten years, he admires the Green Cloud Sect's Lu Xueqi . After his marriage proposal is rejected, he remains concerned that she might be punished for the refusal and requests Yun Yilan to intercede on her behalf. During the Southern Border campaign, he attempts to ambush Ghost Li but fails and ends up in a perilous situation himself. During the events at the Demon-Suppressing Ancient Cave, his primary concern is Lu Xueqi's safety. Later, Li Xun collaborates with Lu Xueqi to pursue the demonic path practitioner Jin Ping'er . Although his aptitude is considered comparable to that of Fa Xiang from the Heavenly Sound Temple, his conduct and methods spark controversy regarding the behavior of righteous sect disciples."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Yan Hong","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"She is his junior sister, and is collectively known with Li Xun as the Twin Heroes of Burning Incense Valley or the Outstanding Disciples of Burning Incense Valley."},{"t":"h","x":"Lu Xueqi","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"He fell in love with her at first sight and remained infatuated with her for ten years, but his feelings were never reciprocated."},{"t":"h","x":"Zeng Shushu","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"He is the cousin of Zeng Shushu of the Qingyun sect. His mother is the eldest daughter of the City Lord of Yuzhou, while Zeng Shushu's mother is the second daughter."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/LiXun-f0448a.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Li_Xun-1ab63c.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Li_Zun_2sx3-111379.png","cap":""}]},"Lin Feng":{"title":"Lin Feng","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[],"ep":10,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"]},"Lin Jingyu":{"title":"Lin Jingyu","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male","aliases":["Lin Jingyu"],"masters":["⟦Cang Song|Cang Song⟧ ⟦Wan Jianyi|Wan Jianyi⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Lin Jingyu is one of the protagonists of Zhu Xian (Jade Dynasty). Grew up with Zhang Xiao in Caomiao Village."},{"t":"p","x":"Always beat Zhang Xiaofan in their sparring when they were young."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Headstrong, hard-working and fiercely loyal to friends."},{"t":"h","x":"Quotes","l":2},{"t":"quote","x":"He was always my best friend and my only brother.","by":""}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive","Human"],"img":"img/wiki/LinzingyuS4-0e88b1.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/LinzingyuS4-d6a807.png","cap":"Season 4"},{"src":"img/wiki/Linjingyus2-8265fb.png","cap":"Season 2"},{"src":"img/wiki/Teenlinjingyu-049080.png","cap":"Teen"},{"src":"img/wiki/Younglinjingyu-7dd75a.png","cap":"Child"}]},"Ling Long":{"title":"Ling Long","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"玲珑","species":["Human"],"gender":"Female","aliases":["Madam Ling Long","巫女娘娘"],"occupation":["Archshamaness"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Linglong (玲珑) is the eleventh generation and the last High Priestess (referred to as the Archshamaness in the donghua) of the Shaman Tribe, possessor of the sacred artifact the Flame Dragon Ring (Xuan Huo Jian), and a master of ancient shamanic arts. In her pursuit of the secret to immortality, she created the ⟦Beast Deity|Beast God⟧ from pure malevolent energy (Li Qi), but developed a forbidden love for him during their time together. When the Beast God spiraled out of control and wreaked havoc upon the mortal realm, she exhausted her life force to seal him within the Demon Suppressing Cave, sacrificing her physical body to grant him a human form—making him mortal upon his eventual resurrection."},{"t":"p","x":"A thousand years later, when the resurrected Beast God is defeated by Zhang Xiaofan and his companions, Linglong’s lingering illusion manifests through the Xuan Huo Jian. She embraces the Beast God as both perish together in the flames of the Eight-Desolation Fire Dragon. Her tragic cycle of creation and destruction stems from her quest to understand the essence of life, bound by an emotional tie that transcends life and death."},{"t":"p","x":"As the last scion of the Shaman civilization, Linglong's choices link together core lore elements like the Xuan Huo Jian and the Eight Ferocious Deities Array. Her tragic sacrifice—sealing the Beast God with her own flesh and blood—runs deep through the secret history of the Southern Border, ultimately resolving a thousand-year karma within the inferno of the Demon Suppressing Cave."}],"ep":53,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/LingLong-Donghua-5a9849.webp","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Linglong-c7a105.webp","cap":"Linglong illustration in the Donghua adaptation season 4"},{"src":"img/wiki/Ling_Long_vanishing-02d223.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Ling_Long-292678.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Lady_Ling_Long-c03994.png","cap":""}]},"Locations":{"title":"Locations","kind":"place","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"[The Divine Land] (神州)","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"The Divine Land is vast and boundless, with the Central Plains naturally being the most prosperous region. Beyond the Central Plains, to the north lies the bitterly cold Arctic Ice Plain, a land of ice and snow, rarely visited by humans. To the east stretches the boundless, vast ocean. As for the south, beyond the Central Plains stand the Ten Thousand Mountains, towering on the border in endless ranges. This area is full of treacherous mountains and vicious rivers, with countless miasmas and poisonous creatures. Legends speak of strange and peculiar savage tribes there, who are said to be bloodthirsty and extremely ferocious."},{"t":"p","x":"To the west of the Divine Land, there are two infamous dangerous areas. In the northwest lies an endless, desolate戈壁 (gobi desert), known to the world as the \"Barbaric Land.\" It sees no rain for a hundred years, and the climate is extremely arid. Although there are occasional oases, they are mostly occupied by fierce beasts and vicious creatures; naturally, any ordinary person entering would be walking to their doom. According to rumors, deep within the Barbaric Land stands a grand temple, which is precisely the birthplace of the Devil Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"As for the southwest, there lies the massive Death Swamp, a place that strikes fear into people's hearts at its mere mention."},{"t":"p","x":"【Changhe City】(昌合城)"},{"t":"p","x":"A relatively sizable city closest to the East Sea. Traveling east from here for another four hundred li leads to the coast of the East Sea."},{"t":"p","x":"【Heyang City】(河阳城)"},{"t":"p","x":"Located fifty li south of Qingyun Mountain, it is the largest and most prosperous place within a hundred-li radius. The city has a population of at least two to three hundred thousand people. Its advantageous location attracts a great number of merchants and travelers."},{"t":"p","x":"【Shanhai Inn】(山海苑)"},{"t":"p","x":"The largest inn in Heyang City is called the Shanhai Inn, which is quite large in scale. Its rear garden is built within a larger garden, with four courtyards situated in the north, south, east, and west directions, serving as the inn's four distinct villas. The Shanhai Inn operates its own restaurant, located on the busiest street in Heyang City. However, the VIP hall on the third floor is exceptionally quiet and spacious, furnished with fewer than ten tables. The second-floor main hall is ornate and magnificent, while the third floor is decorated with carved dragons and painted phoenixes, featuring rosewood beams and an entirely different, classical ambiance compared to the second floor. This is the place where Zhang Xiaofan and Lu Xueqi first arrived after descending the mountain, and it is also where Zhang Xiaofan and Biyao first met."},{"t":"p","x":"The signature dish of the Shanhai Inn is Steamed Sleeper Fish (清蒸寐鱼). The Sleeper Fish was originally a specialty of the Zhugou Mountain in the south, located thousands of li away from Heyang City. A century ago, the Qingyun Sect's Master Daoxuan passed by Zhugou Mountain and specifically brought the Sleeper Fish back, releasing them into the Hongchuan River on the northern shade of Qingyun Mountain. Not only did the fish survive, but they also gradually thrived. It has since become the signature delicacy of the Shanhai Inn."},{"t":"h","x":"Other Locations","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"【义庄】 Temple of Silence"},{"t":"p","x":"【草庙村】 Caomiao Village - Located at the foot of Qingyun Mountain, fifty miles northwest of the big city \"Heyang\". It is home to 42 households and a total of 247 people. Caomiao Village is where Zhang Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu are from."},{"t":"p","x":"【黑石洞】 Black Stone Cave - Located ten li north of Xiaochi Town."},{"t":"p","x":"【火龙洞】 Fire Dragon Cave - Located underground within the Black Stone Cave."},{"t":"p","x":"【三福镇】 Sanfu Town - The nearest inhabited place to Fox Ridge Mountain, a small town about two hundred li to the northeast."},{"t":"p","x":"【空桑山】 Kongsang Mountain - Located three thousand li east of Qingyun Mountain, about a hundred li in radius."},{"t":"p","x":"【万蝠古窟】 Ancient Cave of Ten Thousand Bats - The cave contains millions of giant black bats."},{"t":"p","x":"【滴血洞】 Dripping Blood Cave - Located by the Merciless Sea within the Dead Souls Abyss. Contains: Ancient Corpse Poison, Hehuan Bell, Celestial Book Vol. 1, Spell of Fatal Longing."},{"t":"p","x":"【无情海】 Merciless Sea - One of the Five Seas, hidden deep underground."},{"t":"p","x":"【大王村】 King Village - The closest settlement to the Death Swamp."},{"t":"p","x":"【死亡沼泽】 Death Swamp"},{"t":"p","x":"【天帝宝库】 Celestial Emperor's Treasure Vault"},{"t":"p","x":"【西北蛮荒】 Northwestern Barrens"},{"t":"p","x":"【清泉洲】 Clear Spring Oasis"},{"t":"p","x":"【小湖洲】 Small Lake Oasis"},{"t":"p","x":"【蛮荒圣殿】 Barren Holy Temple"},{"t":"p","x":"【南疆】 Southern Frontier"},{"t":"p","x":"【七里峒】 Seven Li Grotto"},{"t":"p","x":"【天水寨】 Tianshui Stockade"},{"t":"p","x":"【黎族】 Li Tribe"},{"t":"p","x":"【十万大山】 Ten Thousand Mountains"},{"t":"p","x":"【镇魔古洞】 Demon-Subduing Ancient Cave"},{"t":"p","x":"【东海流波山】 Liubo Mountain, East Sea"}]},"Longevity Hall":{"title":"Longevity Hall","kind":"faction","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Longevity Hall (Changsheng Tang, 长生堂) is one of the major sects of the demonic path, once powerful and prestigious but later severely weakened and driven by a desperate struggle for survival; founded on the pursuit of immortality through esoteric and often ruthless means, its methods and legacy are marked by ambition, secrecy, and eventual decline amid the relentless conflicts within the jianghu. The most famous and prominent member of the Longevity Hall is undoubtedly its last leader, Yu Yangzi."}]},"Lu Xueqi":{"title":"Lu Xueqi","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"陆雪琪","species":["Human"],"gender":"Female","aliases":["Xueqi","Qi'er (By ⟦Shui Yue|Shui Yue⟧)","Lady Lu","Senior Sister Lu","Junior Sister Lu","Apprentice Niece Lu (By ⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧)"],"physique":["Tall & thin"],"masters":["⟦Shui Yue|Shui Yue⟧"],"family":["Unnamed mother"],"spouse":["⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧"],"continent":["⟦Shenzou|Shenzou⟧"],"region":["Central Plain"],"occupation":["Disciple of ⟦Qingyun Sect|Qingyun Sect's⟧ Little Bamboo Peak"]},"blocks":[{"t":"quote","x":"Are you the same Zhang Xiaofan from back then?","by":""},{"t":"quote","x":"Come back, junior disciple Zhang","by":""},{"t":"p","x":"Lu Xueqi is the Heroine of Zhu Xian (Jade Dynasty) and the wife of ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧. Currently serving as the head of ⟦Qingyun Sect|Little Bamboo Peak⟧. She is an unparalleled beauty that can captivate the world, resembling a fairy. She is dressed in white with a blue divine sword on her back, her black hair flying, emitting a chilvarous spirit. She is the leader among the new generation of disciples of Qingyun , one of the three major righteous sects. She is highly talented, has deep cultivation, is cold and detached, and doesn't like to talk much."},{"t":"p","x":"She uses a valuable spiritual sword known as Tianya Jian (天琊剑) which was given to her by her master and specializes in lightning spells and techniques (Thunderblade). She cultivate the Taichi Xuanqing Dao."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Lu Xueqi is the most beautiful female in the universe of Zhu Xian, this fact had been emphasized many times by the author through his repeated description of how beautiful she is and his constant comparisons of the other female characters to her. She is described to have a skin as white as snow, a smooth & long black hair, bright & clear pair of eyes with tall nose while her figure is thin and delicate. She is so beautiful that some people had describe her as 'a Fairy from heaven'."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"At first, she was cold, indifferent, competitive, and unyielding. It can be said that Lu Xueqi was not a stereotyped character from the beginning. She was a character that was slowly discovered. Her image gradually became fuller, and her personality became vivid , just like the cold snow will always melt slowly. As time goes by, her independence, infatuation, loyalty, strength, forbearance, intelligence, and calmness are revealed one by one, and her human side, such as devotion, joy, frustration, fragility, optimism, etc., makes her image more flesh and blood, straightforward and measured, mature and unsophisticated."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Originally an orphan that later got adopted by ⟦Shui Yue|Shui Yue⟧ as a disciple of Qingyun Sect. Influenced by her master and the sect's teaching, Lu Xueqi originally aim to be an immortal respected by all, succeed her master as the next Little Bamboo Peak's Head and severe her emotion completely to achieve that, which, at the end, she failed to."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Zhang Xiaofan","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"During the internal Qingyun sect martial arts competition, Zhang Xiaofan continues to win his matches until he gets matched up with ⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧ from Little Bamboo Peak. No one expected him to win against her because she was considered one of the best cultivators within the sect."},{"t":"p","x":"When the fight started Zhang Xiaofan was distracted because he was disappointed that his senior sister, Tian Ling'er, whom he had a crush on, wasn't there to watch his match."},{"t":"p","x":"So Lu Xueqi dominated the fight during the beginning until Xiaofan gets serious and goes on the offensive, using his spiritual weapon to fight back."},{"t":"p","x":"The fight becomes intense as Zhang Xiaofan's eyes become red (likely due to the demonic effect of his artifacts) and he starts to overwhelm Lu Xueqi. Backed into a corner while considering the expectations that her master has placed upon her, Lu Xueqi ends up using her ultimate technique, Mighty Sword of Thunder, despite her injuries."},{"t":"p","x":"But it takes time and just when she is about to summon the thunder, Zhang Xiaofan rushes towards her in a rage to finish the match. When it looks like he will win, since he was just about to reach her (and take her down) before the lightning can hit him, he sees Lu Xueqi as his senior sister, Tian Ling'er."},{"t":"p","x":"He ends up giving up, releasing his grip on his spiritual weapon and Lu Xueqi's technique strikes him down."},{"t":"p","x":"As a result, Lu Xueqi becomes interested in Zhang Xiaofan because she wonders why he gave up the match even though he was about to win. She also doesn't tell anyone about this as she competitive and didn't want words to go out that she the wielder of Tianya sword was defeated with a stick."},{"t":"p","x":"Later on when she, Zhang Xiaofan, Zeng Shushu and Qi Hao descend the mountain to investigate the sighting of demonic cultivators near a certain cave, the group rests in a small town. That same night, Lu Xueqi finds an opportunity to ask Zhang Xiaofan why he gave up the match so easily."},{"t":"p","x":"She asked him if he intentionally gave up the match and in response, Zhang Xiaofan stayed humble, saying that his cultivation was not as good as hers while also thanking her for holding back against him."},{"t":"p","x":"This response confused her and her frozen icy heart started to stir without her knowledge."},{"t":"p","x":"Over time, she slowly develops feelings for him through various encounters and life-and-death situations where Zhang Xiaofan helps her despite being weaker than her."},{"t":"p","x":"When their group was ambushed by those from the ⟦Blood-Refining Guild|Blood-Refining Guild⟧ at Mt. Kongshang, Zhang Xiaofan protects her even though their group was outnumbered. Then when ⟦Nian Lao Da|Nian Lao Da⟧ from the Blood-Refining Guild kicks Zhang Xiaofan off of a cliff, Lu Xueqi jumps down to save him without hesitation."},{"t":"p","x":"They end up landing in a deeper, secluded area of Mt. Kongshang and there are various evil spirits and demonic creatures that were interested in draining their spiritual energy."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan wakes up just in time to rescue Lu Xueqi when she is about to be eaten by a tree-like creature and he helps her recover her energy. Afterwards, Bi Yao interrupts them and a big serpent like creature becomes attracted to their presence."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan knows that she was too weakened to fight so he puts her in a safe place off to the side while he distracts the serpent with Bi Yao."},{"t":"p","x":"The two end up getting split up and Lu Xueqi reunites with Qi Hao and the others (those from Tian Yin Temple and Fen Xiang Valley) while Zhang Xiaofan ends up with Bi Yao in a secret area within the mountain."},{"t":"p","x":"By this point, Lu Xueqi starts to realize what kind of person Zhang Xiaofan is despite what he seems on the outside."},{"t":"p","x":"She returns to Qingyun Sect while Zhang Xiaofan is stuck with Bi Yao within the Kongsang mountain for several days and is unable to focus on her training as her feelings towards Zhang Xiaofan grow stronger."},{"t":"p","x":"When Zhang Xiaofan eventually returns to Qingyun Sect, he finds out that his senior sister, Tian Ling'er is engaged to Qi Hao and he becomes so overwhelmed with hurt and rage that he attacks his senior brother, ⟦Song Daren|Song Daren⟧."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan kneels for punishment and when it starts raining, Lu Xueqi comes over to see him, intending to comfort him. Since he risked his life to protect her, she vowed to do the same for him."},{"t":"quote","x":"Don't be afraid. This will eventually fade with time. I will stand by your side.","by":""},{"t":"p","x":"She understood his struggles and his pain even though no one else seemed to understand him."},{"t":"p","x":"Then when Zhang Xiaofan was accused of being a spy from the Demonic Cults and was about to be arrested, she stepped out to vouch for him. She guaranteed with her life that he could never collude with the evil cultivators. When ⟦Bi Yao|Bi Yao⟧ held ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧'s hands and wlked out of the Qingyun hall she obstructed their path in order to prove that he would be called a traitor if he leaves with her."},{"t":"p","x":"It was also that same day, that he vanished from her life for several years."},{"t":"p","x":"When they met again, it was ten years later and she had completely fallen in love with him even though she knew that they couldn't be together. They were on opposite sides after all."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan was now known as Gui Li (Wandering Ghost) and the deputy of the Ghost King Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"The first thing Zhang Xiaofan asks when they meet again after 10 years, was if she was doing alright. Instead of answering she asks him a question as well, asking him why he didn't kill her. Continuing this tit for tat, Zhang Xiaofan asks her why did she protect him so fiercely back then, in the main hall when he was under trial (and being interrogated by ⟦Dao Xuan|Dao Xuan⟧, the sect leader of ⟦Qingyun Sect|Qingyun Sect⟧)."},{"t":"p","x":"Again, Lu Xueqi doesn't answer but asks another question, asking him if he was still the same person from the past, in order to dodge his questions. She then addresses him as junior brother Zhang and asks him to return back with her. Gui Li finally responds instead of answering a question with a question. He says that he hasn't used that name for a long time (implying that he rejects her offer)."},{"t":"quote","x":"I will, so you better kill me when you get the chance","by":""},{"t":"p","x":"She confesses her love to ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ and then performs sword dance in front of him for the last time in order to cut off her ten years of wishful obsession with him. ⟦Xiao Bai|Xiao Bai⟧ also knew that this was not actually cutting of her ties with him as even though the actions reflected that but her heart didn't. She wanted him to cross the border which she drew before the dance to be surpassed by ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ and return to her side once again. She ultimately rejects a marriage proposal and disobeys her master ⟦Shui Yue|Shui Yue⟧ for the first time because she can't make space for another man in her heart other than Xiaofan. Everyone on Small Bamboo Peak including her master knows that she already has Zhang Xiaofan in her heart but can't refuse the marriage proposal as its a way to unite all sects. Zhang Xiao fan visits her and tells her to leave him with him but her question of asking about Bi Yao stuns him and he leaves."},{"t":"quote","x":"Since then, I remembered you in my heart.","by":""},{"t":"p","x":"When she comes to know that Bi Yao has dissipated she without any thought leaves Small Bamboo Peak in search of ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ in order to console him. She takes care of him when he was in trans and didn't leave his side for days. She was the only one who could understand his inner emotions and sorrow and felt contented that she was able to stay with him. In the end, she becomes Zhang Xiaofan's wife and is seen with him having a son in the epilogue of the novel."},{"t":"h","x":"Shui Yue","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"Lu Xueqi is one of the direct disciples of ⟦Shui Yue|Shui Yue⟧. She treats her like her own daughter."},{"t":"h","x":"Wen Min","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"She is the senior sister of Lu Xueqi and is married to ⟦Song Daren|Song Daren⟧ of the Big Bamboo Peak."}],"ep":5,"ch":23,"tags":["Alive","Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Lu_er-345909.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Luxueqi_s1-d81b08.png","cap":"S1"},{"src":"img/wiki/Her_The_Nine_Heavens_Mysterious_Breaker_turned_into_divine_t-b5de15.jpg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/When_she_reach_Taiqing_Realm-b1d25b.jpg","cap":"Taiqing Realm"},{"src":"img/wiki/Lu_Xueqi-4a06bc.jpg","cap":"FanArt"},{"src":"img/wiki/She_looks_like_a_Phoenix-32570a.jpg","cap":"Fan Art 2"},{"src":"img/wiki/LuXueqiVsZXF-4582fa.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/ZXF_GivesUp-50ec87.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/LuXueqi_Confused-45eb95.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/LuXueqi_DevelopsFeelings-77f67b.png","cap":""}]},"Manhua":{"title":"Manhua","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The manhua version of Zhu Xian is a Chinese comic adaptation of the popular xianxia novel by Xiao Ding. For many fans, it serves as a visual companion to the novel, bringing the epic story to life through detailed artwork."},{"t":"p","x":"There are several versions of manhua that have been circulating. Due to the lack of available information, the fandom only discusses three of them."},{"t":"h","x":"Celestial Destroyer","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"The manhua follows the same core narrative as the novel, chronicling the journey of Zhang Xiaofan, a boy who survives the massacre of his village and is taken in by the prestigious Qing Yun Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"The manhua is primarily known by its original Chinese title, 诛仙 (Zhū Xiān), but is also commonly referred to by its English title, Celestial Destroyer. It was published by Changsha Angel Culture Co., Ltd."},{"t":"p","x":"This manhua version has a chibi/cute style of drawing."},{"t":"h","x":"Celestial Destroyer: Scroll of White Silk Cloud","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"This manhua version was published by China South Angel in 2009."},{"t":"p","x":"INKR states that this is also published by Changsha Angel Culture Co., Ltd. and is a second part, but that's actually not true because the art style is completely different."},{"t":"h","x":"Zhu Xian","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"This version of the manhua was drawn by Ben Wong, a Malaysian artist, and published by Comixo Studio in 2009."},{"t":"p","x":"The comic began serialization on July 18, 2009. There are 151 chapters in total, but never finished, The comic was discontinued due to copyright issues. It was later serialized on Tencent Comics platform under the title \"Zhu Xian: Yu Jian Xing\"."}],"img":"img/wiki/Zhu-xian-ss-bd6327.webp","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Zhu-xian-ss-6590dc.webp","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Celestial-destroyer-manhua-7455cb.webp","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Celestial-Destroyer-193x278-081dc8.webp","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Zhu-xian-comic-68297a.webp","cap":""}]},"Master Puzhi":{"title":"Master Puzhi","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male","disciples":["⟦Zhang_Xiaofan|Zhang_Xiaofan⟧ (Temporary)"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Puzhi is one of the Four Great Divine Monks of the ⟦Tian Yin Temple|Tianyin Temple⟧ in Zhu Xian."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He cultivated the Buddhist Great Brahma Prajna technique and possessed two powerful magical treasures: the Jade Prayer Beads and the Blood-devouring Pearl. His lifelong pursuit was to achieve longevity through the dual cultivation of Buddhism and Daoism."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He made multiple trips to the Qingyun Sect to propose collaboration without success. During his travels, he also studied Daoist techniques and came to believe that the fusion of the five volumes of the Heavenly Scriptures represented the supreme path. Due to prolonged exposure to the Blood-devouring Pearl, he suffered from its evil energy backlash. After being ambushed by Cangsong Daoren in Grass Temple Village and left near death, he imparted the Great Brahma Prajna to Zhang Xiaofan and orchestrated the village massacre to ensure Zhang Xiaofan's entry into the Qingyun Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"On his deathbed, Puzhi confessed his crimes to his senior brother, Puhong, and entrusted Zhang Xiaofan to the care of the Tianyin Temple. A decade later, after Zhang Xiaofan learned the truth and chose forgiveness, Puzhi's remains turned to ashes and dissipated. The character serves as a core vessel of contradiction driving the main plot of Jade Dynasty, shaped by his obsession with dual cultivation and the karmic consequences of the Blood-devouring Pearl."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Monkpuzhi-c9882b.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Puzhi-b6c0ee.png","cap":""}]},"Movie":{"title":"Movie","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Title = Jade Dynasty (2019)"],[1,"Chinese title = 诛仙 1"],[1,"Pinyin = Zhu Xian"],[1,"Also Known as = Noble Aspiration, The Attack of Heaven, Jade Dynasty 1"],[1,"Status = Aired"],[1,"Air Date = Sep 13, 2019"],[1,"Director = Ching Siu Tung"],[1,"Screenwriter = Shen Jie"],[1,"Adapted from = Zhu Xian by Xiao Ding"],[1,"Genres = Xianxia, Fantasy"],[1,"Duration = 1 hr. 41 min."],[1,"Age rating = 13+ (Teens 13 or Older)"],[1,"Type = Movie"]]},{"t":"p","x":"Jade Dynasty is a Live-action movie adaptation of Zhu Xian. Released on September 13, 2019."},{"t":"h","x":"Plot","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"After the massacre of his village, Zhang Xiao Fan is taken in by the Qing Yun Sect, where he begins his journey of cultivation. When he finds out the truth behind the deaths of his parents, he succumbs to his rage and demonic tendencies and becomes the enemy of the Qing Yun Sect."},{"t":"h","x":"Cast & Credits","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Xiao Zhan as Zhang Xiao Fan"],[1,"Li Qin as Lu Xue Qi"],[1,"Meng Mei Qi as Bi Yao"],[1,"Tang Yi Xin as Tian Ling Er"]]}],"img":"img/wiki/-be5cef.jpg","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/JadeDynastyMovie-42ced3.jpg","cap":""}]},"Mr. Ghost":{"title":"Mr. Ghost","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"鬼先生","gender":"Male","aliases":["Ghost Doctor Gui Xiansheng"],"disciples":["⟦Xiao Huan|Xiao Huan⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Mr. Ghost (鬼先生), also known as the Ghost Doctor, is a mysterious character in the novel Zhu Xian."},{"t":"h","x":"Apperance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Dressed entirely in black, with a black veil covering his face, he exudes a ghostly aura and an indescribable eeriness."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is a retainer of the Ghost King Sect of the Demonic Cult, proficient in ghost arts, and over three hundred years old. He is always dressed in black and wears a mask, assisting the Ghost King in deciphering the inscriptions on the Fulong Cauldron and overseeing the Four Spirits Blood Array."},{"t":"p","x":"As a complex character whose morality is difficult to distinguish as simply good or evil, he ruthlessly carried out various conspiracies while also showing remorse for his deceased friends and concern for preserving his legacy. He ultimately perished in the very blood array he had planned."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He once saved Wan Jianyi's severed arm and gave Puzhi a Three-Day Death Pill, but during the Battle of Qingyun, he ambushed Wan Jianyi and killed him."},{"t":"p","x":"Because he admired Zhou Xiaohuan's talent in the Ghost Path, he made an exception and accepted her as his disciple, giving her a Blood Jade Bone Fragment and a secret technique. Mr. Ghost ultimately became a sacrifice to the Asura (Xiu Luo/ Shura / 修罗). On his deathbed, he entrusted Zhang Xiaofan with the task of finding Xiao Huan in order to save Qingyun Mountain."},{"t":"h","x":"External Links","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Baidu"]]}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/MrGhost-69ab7f.webp"},"Mystic Fire Mirror":{"title":"Mystic Fire Mirror","kind":"item","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Xuanhuo Mirror (玄火鉴, literally Mystic Fire Mirror) is an ancient divine artifact from the novel Zhu Xian. It originally belonged to the southern witch ⟦Ling Long|Linglong⟧, and later became the guardian treasure of Burning Incense Valley. Its appearance is that of a jade-green ring, with a thin plate inlaid at the center bearing a crimson flame totem, and red tassels hanging from both sides. It is classified as a supreme Yang-type magical weapon."},{"t":"p","x":"The Xuanhuo Mirror embodies the essence of ten thousand fires, capable of summoning Fire Dragon of the Eight Desolations (八荒火龙 ). When combined with the “Eight Fierce Profound Fire Formation” within the Xuanhuo Altar, it can unleash a power strong enough to destroy heaven and earth, and during the War of the Beast God it once burned away his physical body. Its pure Yang energy can suppress the backlash of the Soul-Devouring Staff, as well as subdue the Scarlet Flame Demon Beast and rescue the Nine-Tailed Celestial Fox. The power of this artifact is considered second only to ancient divine relics such as the Zhuxian Sword and the Fulong Cauldron."},{"t":"p","x":"Owners: Ling Long → Fanxian Valley → Nine-Tailed Heavenly Fox → Six-Tailed Fox → Zhang Xiaofan (Gui Li)"},{"t":"p","x":"Also known as:"},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"玄火鉴"],[1,"Xuanhuo Mirror"],[1,"Xuan Huo Jian"],[1,"Flame Dragon Ring"]]}]},"Nian Lao Da":{"title":"Nian Lao Da","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[],"ep":10,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/NianLaoDa-7f9e2b.png"},"Novel":{"title":"Novel","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"\"Zhu Xian\" (mandarin: 诛仙, english: Jade Dynasty) is a long-length xianxia novel created by contemporary author Xiao Ding. The novel was written approximately between 2003 and 2007. It was first published in Taiwan, China in March 2003. In April 2005, the first six volumes were published by Zhaohua Publishing House in mainland China, while the last two volumes were subsequently published by Huashan Literature and Art Publishing House."},{"t":"p","x":"The novel, centered around the theme \"Heaven and Earth are ruthless, and treat the myriad creatures as straw dogs,\" tells the growth story of an ordinary young man named ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ at the foot of Qingyun Mountain. The entire novel is ingeniously conceived and grand in scale, creating a uniquely captivating eastern xianxia legendary universe. With its tumultuous plot and distinct characters, it intertwines love, family bonds, and friendship with the epic struggle between good and evil and battles of destiny. The elegant writing and vivid storytelling have made it a masterpiece. Along with \"Piao Miao Zhi Lü\" and \"Xiao Bing Yi Chuan,\" it is known as one of the \"Three Great Internet Novels\" and is also hailed as the \"Martial Arts Bible of the Post-Jin Yong Era.\""},{"t":"p","x":"In November 2016, \"Zhu Xian\" was selected for the \"Top 10 Internet Literature List - China IP Value List\" at the 2016 China Entertainment Index Festival. On July 12, 2017, it was ranked 14th on the \"2017 Mao Pian·Hurun Original Literature IP Value List.\" In August 2018, at China's \"Internet Literature+\" Conference, it was recognized as one of the \"20 High-Quality IPs in the Development History of Internet Literature.\""},{"t":"p","x":"On May 13, 2024, the original author Xiao Ding announced that the newly revised edition of his classic work \"Zhu Xian\" has been released on Qidian Reader. This marks the first revision since the novel's initial publication, resulting from years of the author's contemplation and refinement."},{"t":"p","x":"There are 256 chapters and the total word count is about 1.2 million characters in total."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhu Xian, together with ⟦Zhu Xian II (Novel)|Zhu Xian II⟧ and ⟦Savage Journey (Prequel Novel)|Savage Journey⟧ (the prequel to Zhu Xian), form the Zhu Xian Trilogy."},{"t":"p","x":"Other novels by Xiao Ding that related to Zhu Xian (Shared Universe) are 戮仙 (Lù Xiān) and 天影 (Tiān Yǐng)."}],"img":"img/wiki/Novel-929175.webp"},"Pu Hong":{"title":"Pu Hong","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Puhong is the abbot of Tianyin Temple in the novel Zhu Xian."},{"t":"p","x":"He is the foremost of the Four Great Divine Monks and is regarded as the strongest figure in the righteous faction after ⟦Dao Xuan|Daoxuan Zhenren⟧ of Qingyun Sect. He is also one of the representative figures of the three major Buddhist cultivation sects."},{"t":"p","x":"During the battles against the Beast God and the Ghost King, Puhong demonstrated a level of cultivation superior to that of ⟦Yun Yi Lan|Yun Yilan⟧ of Incense Valley (Fen Xiang Valley). Following the Battle of the Beast God, he temporarily assumed leadership of the righteous factions after Daoxuan's disappearance. He eventually retired from the martial world and entrusted Tianyin Temple to his disciple, Faxiang."},{"t":"p","x":"Because of the massacre committed by ⟦Master Puzhi|Puzhi⟧ of Tianyin Temple, Puhong once saved Zhang Xiaofan's life at Qingyun Mountain. He later helped Zhang Xiaofan dispel the baleful energy within him through the Wordless Jade Bi, enabling him to comprehend the fourth volume of the Book of Heaven."},{"t":"p","x":"His magical treasure is the Great Compassion Golden Wheel. Tianyin Temple is based on the Buddhist cultivation technique Brahma Prajna and places particular emphasis on defense and Buddhist cultivation. It is one of the major forces of the righteous faction in the fight against the beast demons."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[]},"Qi Hao":{"title":"Qi Hao","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male","aliases":["Qi Hao (齐昊)"],"spouse":["⟦Tian Ling'er|Tian Ling'er⟧"]},"blocks":[],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/QiHao-b10457.png"},"Qi Xiaoxuan":{"title":"Qi Xiaoxuan","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"齐小萱","species":["Human"],"gender":"Female","masters":["⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧"],"family":["⟦Qi Hao|Qi Hao⟧ (Father)","⟦Tian Ling'er|Tian Ling'er⟧ (Mother)"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Qi Xiaoxuan (齐小萱) is an important character in the novel Zhu Xian II, she is the daughter of ⟦Qi Hao|Qi Hao⟧ , the head of Longshou Peak of the Qingyun Sect, and ⟦Tian Ling'er|Tian Ling'er⟧ . She inherited her parents' excellent lineage and had mastered the third level of Tai Chi Xuan Qing Dao by the age of eleven."},{"t":"p","x":"Her cultivation has reached the seventh level of the Jade Pure Realm, making her a once-in-a-century cultivation prodigy for the Qingyun Sect . The sect's elders hold high hopes for her, believing she is the disciple most likely to break through the shackles of cultivation since Lu Xueqi."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Qi Xiaoxuan's appearance is as if delicately carved from jade, clearly a beauty in the making."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"A lively and active personality, though occasionally timid."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive","Human"]},"Qin Wuyan":{"title":"Qin Wuyan","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"秦无炎","gender":"Male","aliases":["Young Poison Master, 毒公子(Du Gonzi), Third Young Master of Ghost King Sect"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Qin Wuyan (秦无炎) is an important character in the novels Zhu Xian and Zhu Xian II."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"As the outstanding figure among the younger generation of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect, he lives up to his name and his sect, being cold, ruthless, and venomous, as well as meticulous, scheming, arrogant, and unyielding."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is the closed-door disciple of Poison God, the sect master of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect, one of the four major factions of the Demon Sect, and one of the Three Princes of the Demon Sect, known as the 'Poison Prince'."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"In ' Zhu Xian ', after the death of Poison God, the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect fell into internal strife. Remembering Poison God's dying instructions, Qin Wuyan did not participate in the struggle for sect leadership. In the storyline of the third season of 'Zhu Xian', Poison God entrusted the sect master's token to Qin Wuyan on his deathbed, allowing Qin Wuyan to smoothly become the new sect master of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect. Qin Wuyan harbors deep affection for Bi Yao , the daughter of the Ghost King Sect's master. In an attempt to resurrect Bi Yao, he used a ruse of self-inflicted injury to infiltrate the Incense Burning Valley, but was later captured, persecuted, and had his cultivation destroyed. In ' Zhu Xian II ', Qin Wuyan establishes a branch sect of the Demon Sect called the Yin Demon Sect and becomes its master."},{"t":"p","x":"In the story of ' Zhu Xian ', he feigned death and disappeared after the Battle of Poison Snake Valley. Afterwards, he vanished without a trace, taking with him the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect's hereditary token, the Ten Thousand Poisons Divine Seal, and his fate remains a mystery."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/QinWuyan-51e578.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Qin_Wuyan-97d83c.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Qin_Wuyan_2x2_2-3aef8e.png","cap":""}]},"Qing Long":{"title":"Qing Long","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[],"ep":20,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"]},"Qingyun Sect":{"title":"Qingyun Sect","kind":"faction","facts":{"zh":"青云门","type":"Righteous","status":"Active","founder":["⟦Qingyunzi|Qingyunzi⟧"],"members":["⟦Xiao Yicai|Xiao Yicai⟧","⟦Qi Hao|Qi Hao⟧","⟦Lin Jingyu|Lin Jingyu⟧","⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧","⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ (former)","⟦Zeng Shushu|Zeng Shushu⟧","⟦Wen Min|Wen Min⟧","⟦Tian Ling'er|Tian Ling'er⟧"],"allies":["⟦Tian Yin Temple|Tian Yin Temple⟧","⟦Fen Xiang Valley|Fen Xiang Valley⟧"],"enemies":["⟦Ghost King Sect|Ghost King Sect⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Description","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Pronunciation: Qing Yun Men - 青云门"},{"t":"p","x":"One of the most prestigious and largest sects in the martial world. Known to be the best \"righteous\" sect."},{"t":"h","x":"Location","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Qingyun Mountain (青云山): The sect is headquartered on a majestic and spiritually potent mountain range. The mountain is famously described as having seven main peaks, each serving a specific function and led by a peak elder."],[1,"The Seven Peaks: The most important among them are:"],[2,"通天峰 (Tōngtiān Fēng - \"Peak that Reaches Heaven\"): The main peak and the seat of the sect leader. It houses the main hall and the most important ceremonies are held here."],[2,"大竹峰 (Dàzhú Fēng - \"Big Bamboo Peak\"): Known for its vast bamboo forests. This is the home peak of the protagonist, Zhang Xiaofan, and his master, Tian Buyi. It's often portrayed as more rustic and close-knit compared to the others."],[2,"小竹峰 (Xiǎozhú Fēng - \"Small Bamboo Peak\"): Traditionally the peak for female disciples. Lu Xueqi, the female lead, is from this peak."],[2,"龙首峰 (Lóngshǒu Fēng - \"Dragon Head Peak\"): A powerful and prestigious peak, known for its strict discipline. Key characters like Qi Hao and his master, Cang Song, are from here."],[2,"风回峰 (Fēnghuí Fēng - \"Peak of Whirling Winds\"): The home of Zeng Shushu, a close friend of Zhang Xiaofan."],[2,"朝阳峰 (Cháoyáng Fēng - \"Morning Sun Peak\")"],[2,"落霞峰 (Luòxiá Fēng - \"Setting Rosy Clouds Peak\")"]]}],"img":"img/wiki/Qingyun_sect-e63698.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Elderqingyunsect-fb0fb2.webp","cap":"Elders of Qingyun sect"}]},"Qingyunzi":{"title":"Qingyunzi","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"青云子","species":["Human"],"gender":"Male","occupation":["Fortune Teller (early life)","Founding Master of Qingyun Sect"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Qingyunzi (青云子) is a character in the novel Zhu Xian. Originally a fortune-teller who traveled the martial world, he began cultivating the Dao after obtaining an unnamed ancient scripture on Qingyun Mountain at the age of 49. He founded the ⟦Qingyun Sect|Qingyun Sect⟧, which would become the leader of the righteous path, and served as its first sect leader. He lived to the age of 367."},{"t":"p","x":"The Taiji Xuanqing Dao, a cultivation method he developed, became the Qingyun Sect's core cultivation technique. The magical artifacts and protective restrictions he left behind repeatedly helped the sect survive crises. However, of the ten disciples he taught, only one lineage survived due to natural disasters and human calamities. As a result, the Qingyun Sect went through approximately four centuries of decline before being revitalized by ⟦Daoist Qingye|Daoist Qingye⟧."},{"t":"p","x":"The novel repeatedly hints that his lineage may not have died out completely. The wandering fortune-teller ⟦Zhou Yi Xian|Zhou Yixian⟧ possesses a unique earth-escape technique created by Qingyunzi and refers to himself using titles such as “Patriarch Qingyunzi” and “Patriarch Qingye,” suggesting that he belongs to a separate branch of the same lineage as the Qingyun Sect."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"]},"Races":{"title":"Races","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"【Wu Tribe】","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Also known as the Black Wu Tribe, Ancient Wu Tribe, the Ancient Witch Clan, the Black Witch Clan, or Ancient Wu Shaman Tribe of the Southern Border (南疆古巫族)."},{"t":"p","x":"Long, long ago, the Miao, Li, Zhuang, Tu, and Gaoshan tribes were actually one ancient tribe called the \"Wu Tribe.\""},{"t":"p","x":"According to tribal legends, in ancient times, the Ancient Wu Tribe managed the Southern Border frontiers. They were powerful, and generations produced individuals with profound shamanic powers. Among them, the most powerful in sorcery was the Witch Maiden who served the Witch God in each generation. The so-called Witch Maiden was a virgin selected from within the Ancient Wu Tribe in each generation, possessing the highest innate spiritual power. She would serve the Witch God in the altar, delve into sorcery, and lead all the people of the Wu Tribe."},{"t":"h","x":"【Merman】","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Also known as Merfolk, Yu Ren, 鱼人, Fishman Tribe"},{"t":"p","x":"One of the sixty-three barbarian tribes of the Southern Border. They have fish heads and human bodies. According to their own legends, they are the descendants born from the union of the ancient Fish God and human women, hence they have always considered themselves the descendants of the Fish God. This heterodox tribe has always been cruel and fond of killing. They believe that whether it's an animal or a human, after slaughter, only by chopping and shattering the corpse can the ghost be simultaneously shredded and killed, eliminating future troubles."},{"t":"h","x":"【Yao】","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"One of the sixty-three barbarian tribes of the Southern Border. Resembles a wild duck, about the height of a person. Its body is cyan-colored with light red eyes and a red tail. It has fangs in its mouth and two wings on its back."},{"t":"h","x":"[Fox Demon Clan]","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Three-Tailed Fox Demon","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"A fox demon that has cultivated for three hundred years, able to take human form and charm mortals."},{"t":"h","x":"Six-Tailed Spirit (Demon) Fox","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"A fox demon that has cultivated for a thousand years, thus growing six tails. It is intelligent and cunning, capable of transforming into countless forms."},{"t":"h","x":"Nine-Tailed Heavenly Fox","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"A heterodox race of fox demons. Upon cultivating for five thousand years, they grow nine tails. They are exquisitely enchanting and captivating. Some take human form, maintaining their youthful appearance and achieving longevity. Their magical power can reach divine levels. A peerless demonic creature."}]},"San Miao":{"title":"San Miao","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Female","aliases":["三妙仙子","Fairy San Miao"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"San Miao Xian Zi (三妙仙子), also known as Lady San Miao or Fairy San Miao, is the leader of ⟦HeHuan Sect|Hehuan Sect⟧, one of the four major sects of the Demon Sect, and the master of ⟦Jin Ping'er|Jin Ping'er⟧. She perished during the Beast Tide Incident triggered by the Beast God , directly leading to the downfall of the Hehuan Sect. Her direct disciple, Jin Ping'er, inherited her magical artifact, the \"Purple Edge,\" and her unique skill, the \"Charm Heart Technique,\" but did not succeed her as the sect leader. The demise of this character became a crucial background element driving Jin Ping'er's subsequent plotlines, such as joining other sects and seeking the Fire Phoenix Flame Jade."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"San Miao Xianzi is exceptionally beautiful. According to the original novel's description, she is naturally of rare beauty, yet there is not the slightest hint of vulgarity in her appearance; her complexion is pale, she wears no makeup, and instead possesses an icy, ethereal grace, somewhat reminiscent of Lu Xueqi from Lesser Bamboo Peak on Mount Qingyun."},{"t":"p","x":"Though over fifty years old, her aging has slowed due to her cultivation. For many years, San Miao Xianzi has retained the youthful appearance of a sixteen-year-old girl. Furthermore, through practicing the techniques of the Hehuan Sect, her charm and allure have naturally far surpassed what they were before."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/SanMiaoXianZi-b1b8ea.png"},"Savage Journey (Prequel Novel)":{"title":"Savage Journey (Prequel Novel)","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Savage Journey is a classical xianxia novel written by Xiao Ding, also known as \"A Prequel to Zhu Xian\". It primarily tells the story of the younger days of Tian Buyi and others — who later become Zhang Xiaofan’s masters in Zhu Xian. The work was first serialized in 2007 in the magazine Fantasy Alliance (幻想盟), edited by Xiao Ding, with a total of eight chapters published before the magazine was discontinued. On July 31, 2016, the novel resumed serialization on Qidian Chinese Network (起点中文网) and has since been completed."},{"t":"p","x":"Savage Journey (the prequel to Zhu Xian), together with Zhu Xian and Zhu Xian II, form the Zhu Xian Trilogy."}]},"Sects":{"title":"Sects","kind":"faction","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Righteous Sects","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Qingyun Sect|Qingyun Sect⟧"],[1,"⟦Tian Yin Temple|Tian Yin Temple⟧"],[1,"⟦Fen Xiang Valley|Fen Xiang Valley⟧"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Demonic Sects","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Ghost King Sect|Ghost King Sect⟧, One of the four major factions of the Demonic Cult"],[1,"⟦Blood-Refining Guild|Blood-Refining Guild⟧"],[1,"⟦Ten Thousand Poisons Sect|Ten Thousand Poisons Sect⟧, One of the four major factions of the Demonic Cult"],[1,"⟦Longevity Hall|Longevity Hall⟧ (长生堂 / Chang Sheng Tang), One of the four major factions of the Demonic Cult"],[1,"⟦HeHuan Sect|HeHuan Sect⟧, One of the four major factions of the Demonic Cult"],[1,"Ghost Path (鬼道 / Gui Dao)"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Neutral Factions","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Yu Du City|Yu Du City⟧"]]}]},"Shang Guan Ce":{"title":"Shang Guan Ce","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[],"ep":40,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive","Human"]},"Shang Zhengliang":{"title":"Shang Zhengliang","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male","titles":["Head of Rising Sun Peak"]},"blocks":[],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Shangzhengliang-4c1baf.png"},"Shui Yue":{"title":"Shui Yue","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Female","titles":["Head of Little Bamboo Peak"],"disciples":["⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧","⟦Wen Min|Wen Min⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Shui Yue, also known as Master Shuiyue, is a character in the novel Zhu Xian and its prequel Manhuang Xing. She served as the seventh-generation head of Xiaozhu Peak of the Qingyun Sect and was the master of ⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧ and ⟦Wen Min|Wen Min⟧."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She wore a moon-white Taoist robe, had an oval face, and appeared to be in her thirties. She wielded the Tianya Divine Sword."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Cold and indifferent towards men. Treats her direct disciples warmly. Doesn't accept male disciples."},{"t":"p","x":"Shuiyue has a stern and aloof temperament but cares deeply for her disciples."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"In the past she had a lover who rejected her and from then on, she hated men."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Lu Xueqi","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"She treats Lu Xueqi as if she was her own daughter and has high expectations of her. She just wants her to focus on becoming the strongest cultivator and nothing else. Gave her the Tianya Jian because she saw how much potential she has and wants to teach her everything she knows."},{"t":"h","x":"Wen Min","l":4},{"t":"p","x":"Another one of her disciples but Lu Xueqi is definitely her favorite disciple."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/Shuiyue-13afb5.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Shuo_Yue_2-769136.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Shuo_Yue__2-13da92.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Shuo_Yue-ca4ffe.png","cap":""}]},"Sinister Bead":{"title":"Sinister Bead","kind":"item","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Sinister Bead or Blood-devouring Pearl (噬血珠) is an extremely malevolent magical artifact from the novel Jade Dynasty (Zhu Xian). Originally owned by the Demon Faction's Black-Hearted Old Man, it can absorb the essence and blood of living beings to nourish itself. It was once sealed for thirty years by the divine Buddhist monk Pu Zhi using secret Buddhist arts, who then passed it to ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧. Ultimately, it fused with the Soul-Absorbing Staff (Shehun) through blood-refining to become the Soul-Consuming Staff (Shihun Bang)."},{"t":"p","x":"As one of the Four Treasures of the Demon Faction, this pearl triggered conflicts between good and evil due to the countless slaughters committed by the ⟦Black-Hearted Old Man|Black-Hearted Old Man⟧. After discovering it in the Western Great Swamp, ⟦Master Puzhi|Pu Zhi⟧ suppressed its malevolent nature using jade prayer beads and entrusted it to Zhang Xiaofan before his death. By a stroke of fate, the Blood-Sucking Pearl merged with the Soul-Absorbing Staff in the rear mountains of Qingyun to form the Soul-Consuming Staff, an artifact possessing both righteous and evil powers that became a key token in Zhang Xiaofan's transformation."},{"t":"p","x":"Alternative Names:"},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"噬血珠"],[1,"Shìxuèzhū"],[1,"Blood-Sucking Bead"],[1,"Sinister Orb"],[1,"Bloodthirsty Pearl"],[1,"Bloodthirsty Bead"]]}],"img":"img/wiki/Sinisterbead-c3a96a.png"},"Song Daren":{"title":"Song Daren","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male","titles":["Head Disciple of Big Bamboo Peak"],"aliases":["宋大仁"],"masters":["⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧"],"spouse":["⟦Wen Min|Wen Min⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Song Daren is a male character in the Jade Dynasty and its sequel, Jade Dynasty II. He is the eldest disciple of ⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧, the head of the Great Bamboo Peak of the Qingyun Sect, and the martial brother of Zhang Xiaofan."}],"ep":2,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive","Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Songdaren-c4e259.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Song_Daren-135eca.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Song_Daren_2-16565f.png","cap":""}]},"Spiritual Beasts":{"title":"Spiritual Beasts","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Lingzun (灵尊)","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Over six thousand years old. The Guardian of Qingyun Sect. A water qilin (Chinese mythical creature) that watches over the sect."},{"t":"p","x":"When Zhang Xiaofan arrived at the sect for the very first time, the sinister bead in his possession triggered the creature's animosity."},{"t":"h","x":"Xiao Hui","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan's animal companion. It's a special type of monkey that can open its third eye (in the middle of its forehead) when it fully matures."},{"t":"h","x":"Taotie","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Taotie (饕餮) is an ancient mythical beast in the novel \"Zhu Xian\". It is depicted as a ferocious beast with four eyes, six teeth, and black, hard, bumpy skin. As the companion spirit beast of the Beast God, Taotie followed the Beast God into the Central Plains after the seal on the Ten Thousand Mountains was broken, participating in the decisive battle at the Xuanhuo Altar. Its core plot value lies in being captured by the Ghost King Sect and becoming the energy source of the Four Spirits Blood Array, forming the foundation of the Fulong Cauldron Array together with the Yellow Bird, Kui Niu, and Zhulong.Ultimately, the Ghost King extracted all his spiritual energy, and he perished as a sacrifice to the Four Spirits Blood Array."},{"t":"h","x":"Da Huang / Dahuang","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Dahuang (大黄) is a fictional character in \"Zhu Xian\" and its sequel. Originally, he was a yellow dog raised by Tian Buyi, the head of Dazhu Peak of Qingyun Sect. Later, he became the loyal companion of the protagonist Zhang Xiaofan (Gui Li) and continued to accompany his son Zhang Xiaoding in \"Zhu Xian II\".The character is known as the \"enlightened old dog,\" and appears throughout the original trilogy, forming an emotional bond connecting the two generations of protagonists."},{"t":"h","x":"Kui Niu","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Kui Niu is an ancient mythical beast, resembling a blue ox, with three legs and no horns, its roar like thunder. It dwells in the deep sea, emerging only once every three thousand years. Its emergence is accompanied by storms and lightning; it is known as the mount of the Thunder God. It has very poor eyesight and its body is as large as a small mountain."},{"t":"h","x":"Yellow Bird","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"An ancient divine beast, a spirit bird of the nine heavens, with orange-yellow feathers all over its body and a wingspan of nearly a hundred feet. It protects the spiritual medicines of the eight directions on behalf of the Heavenly Emperor and intimidates the Xuan Snake."},{"t":"h","x":"Crimson Flame Beast & Fire Dragon of Eight Desolations","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Both beasts are related to ⟦Artifacts|Mystic Fire Mirror⟧ (玄火鉴) and ⟦Eight Fiends Formation|Eight Fiends Formation⟧ (八凶玄火法阵)."},{"t":"p","x":"Crimson Flame Beast (赤焰魔兽) = The guardian beast of the Myriad Fires Essence ⟦Artifacts|Mystic Fire Mirror⟧, its body wreathed in crimson flames, raging with fiery poison that instantly kills anyone struck. Legend has it that it possesses heretical secret techniques, and that an ancient, malevolent god used the Crimson Flame Beast to power the ⟦Eight Fiends Formation|Eight Fiends Formation⟧ (八凶玄火法阵), making it extremely eerie."},{"t":"p","x":"Eight-Desolation Fire Dragon aka. Fire Dragons of the Eight Desolations (八荒火龙) = a terrifying legendary beast capable of destroying all creation."},{"t":"h","x":"Source","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Baike Baidu"]]}],"img":"img/wiki/SuiZilin-bd6069.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Xiaohui-14cdcc.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Taotie-b4d7db.jpeg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Firedragonof8desolates-054e6c.webp","cap":""}]},"Su Ru":{"title":"Su Ru","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Female","aliases":["苏茹"],"spouse":["⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Wife of ⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧ and mother of ⟦Tian Ling'er|Tian Ling'er⟧."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Strong, but gentle, acting as a mother figure to all of the disciples at Big Bamboo Peak."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Suru-13eaca.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Su_Ru-ad92d5.png","cap":""}]},"Taotie":{"title":"Taotie","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Taotie (饕餮) is an ancient mythical beast in the novel \"Zhu Xian\". It is depicted as a ferocious beast with four eyes, six teeth, and black, hard, bumpy skin. As the companion spirit beast of the ⟦Beast Deity|Beast God⟧, Taotie followed the Beast God into the Central Plains after the seal on the Ten Thousand Mountains was broken, participating in the decisive battle at the Xuanhuo Altar. Its core plot value lies in being captured by the Ghost King Sect and becoming the energy source of the Four Spirits Blood Array, forming the foundation of the Fulong Cauldron Array together with the Yellow Bird, Kui Niu, and Zhulong.Ultimately, the Ghost King extracted all his spiritual energy, and he perished as a sacrifice to the Four Spirits Blood Array."}],"img":"img/wiki/Taotie-b4d7db.jpeg"},"Ten Thousand Poisons Sect":{"title":"Ten Thousand Poisons Sect","kind":"faction","facts":{"zh":"万毒门","type":"Demonic","status":"Active","members":["⟦Qin Wuyan|Qin Wuyan⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Description","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Pronounication: Wan Du Men - 万毒门"},{"t":"p","x":"A demonic cultivation sect that specializes in poisons"}]},"Tian Buyi":{"title":"Tian Buyi","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"田不易","species":["Human"],"gender":"Male","titles":["Head of Big Bamboo Peak"],"disciples":["⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧","⟦Song Daren|Song Daren⟧"],"spouse":["⟦Su Ru|Su Ru⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Tian Buyi is in charge of Da Zhu Fen (Big Bamboo Peak) in Qingyun Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan was forced upon him because no one else wanted to take Zhang Xiaofan in. His peak is also known to have the disciples with strange quirks (in terms of cultivation artifacts)."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is short and stout in appearance and unremarkable-looking."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Stubborn, pretends not to take when in fact he does care for his disciples. Cares for his wife and sacrificed his life for her."},{"t":"p","x":"His character is tenacious, and his inner excellence manifests externally. Stern in appearance and highly concerned with face, he is inwardly protective of his own and deeply cares for his disciples. He is unequivocal on matters of principle, possessing a strong sense of justice and responsibility."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is the seventh-generation head of Dazhu Peak in the Qingyun Sect ."},{"t":"h","x":"Quotes","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"\"For what purpose does one cultivate throughout a lifetime? How can a man shrink from battle when the time comes?\""},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Zhang Xiaofan","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan is his last disciple."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Tianbuyi-178209.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Tian_Buyi__2-10aa91.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Tian_Buyi-3d525a.png","cap":""}]},"Tian Ling'er":{"title":"Tian Ling'er","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Female","spouse":["⟦Qi Hao|Qi Hao⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Daughter of ⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧, senior martial sister of ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ and Xiaofan's first crush."},{"t":"p","x":"Tian Ling'er is one of the core female characters created by Xiao Ding in Jade Dynasty. The author Xiao Ding has pointed out that Tian Ling'er is an important character who greatly influences the fate and emotions of the protagonist Zhang Xiaofan . In terms of narrative function, Tian Ling'er is portrayed as Zhang Xiaofan's first love and \"White Moonlight,\" and her existence symbolizes the inevitable farewell to an era of innocence in Zhang Xiaofan's growth process."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Cloud-like elegant hair bun, a red silk ribbon tied at her waist, large, sparkling eyes, and two small dimples on her cheeks."},{"t":"p","x":"She is often seen in a red dress, with skin as white as jade, bright and expressive eyes, and a clever, charming demeanor. Her beauty is likened to the summer sun, brimming with youthful vitality and exuberant life force. During the Seven Peaks Competition, she and Lu Xueqi were considered equally brilliant, and they were collectively referred to as the \"Two Beauties\"."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Tian Ling'er is innocent, lively, and adorable. When she was younger, she stood up for Zhang Xiaofan, acting like an older sister figure."},{"t":"p","x":"A little mischievous but has a kind heart and is loyal to those she cares about."},{"t":"p","x":"She possesses a kind-hearted, straightforward, and innocent personality with a pure heart. Having grown up being deeply cherished, she did not develop a domineering temperament. Instead, she is righteous and loves to champion the cause of justice, showing great care and affection for her fellow disciples."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She is the daughter of Tian Buyi and Su Ru, the heads of Dazhu Peak of the Qingyun Sect , and is the senior sister and childhood crush of the male protagonist, Zhang Xiaofan . Tian Ling'er grew up doted on and is relatively intelligent. She is innocent and carefree, lively and charming, and is the beloved younger sister of all her senior brothers at Dazhu Peak."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"After Zhang Xiaofan joins Dazhu Peak, Tian Ling'er becomes his senior martial sister. The two spend their days together, and she often stands up for Zhang Xiaofan when he is bullied, while he develops his first crush and harbors a secret affection for her. Her magical treasure, the \"Amber Vermillion Ribbon,\" was a treasure used by her mother, Su Ru, in her youth. Tian Ling'er and Lu Xueqi were considered equally brilliant during the Seven Peaks Competition. She fell in love with Qi Hao, the chief disciple of Longshou Peak, but their relationship was not approved by her parents, Tian Buyi and Su Ru. She later married Qi Hao."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Qi Hao","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"Tian Ling'er ultimately married Qi Hao, becoming the wife of the head of Longshou Peak, and they had a daughter named Qi Xiaoxuan. After her marriage, she gradually faded from the main storyline, but her existence profoundly influenced Zhang Xiaofan 's fate and emotions."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/Teentianlinger-6ee807.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Tianlinger-07e739.png","cap":"Child"},{"src":"img/wiki/Tian_Ling_er_1-f4af54.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Tian_Ling_er_3-654677.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Tian_Ling_er_4-8ad2e0.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Tian_Ling_er_5-24f444.png","cap":""}]},"Tian Yin Temple":{"title":"Tian Yin Temple","kind":"faction","facts":{"zh":"天音阁","type":"Righteous","status":"Active","members":["⟦Fa Xiang|Fa Xiang⟧","⟦Master Puzhi|Master Puzhi⟧"],"enemies":["⟦Ghost King Sect|Ghost King Sect⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Description","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Pronounciation: Tian Yin Si - 天音阁"},{"t":"p","x":"One of the most reputable temples that believe in good karma and righteous deeds."}]},"Tian Yun":{"title":"Tian Yun","kind":"character","facts":{"titles":["Head of Sunset Peak"]},"blocks":[],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Tianyun-5a45c4.png"},"Tu Ma Gu":{"title":"Tu Ma Gu","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[],"ep":49,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive","Human"]},"Wan Jianyi":{"title":"Wan Jianyi","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"A mysterious man that lives within the vicinity of the Qingyun Sect. Wan Jianyi was a disciple of the Qingyun Sect, one of the three major orthodox sects and the leader of the righteous path. He was an eighteenth-generation disciple of the Qingyun Sect. In his youth, he and the sect leader, Dao Xuan, were known as the \"Twin Pride of Qingyun.\" He wore snow-white robes and possessed extraordinarily handsome features, carrying himself with an air of boldness and heroism. His personality was resolute, bold, and unrestrained, often guided by the belief that \"righteousness in heaven and earth endures forever.\""},{"t":"p","x":"He was secretly admired by Shuiyue, a disciple of Xiaozhu Peak, but his own affections lay with her junior sect sister, Su Ru. After witnessing Su Ru's relationship with Tian Buyi, though heartbroken, he sincerely wished them happiness. During a chaotic battle, he had his left arm severed by Zhuque, one of the Four Saints of the Demon Sect. Despite blood gushing from the wound, he remained composed, even reaching out to remove Zhuque's veil and praising her exceptional beauty—an act that earned her secret admiration for a century."},{"t":"p","x":"A hundred years earlier, he was sentenced to death for killing the demon-possessed Tianchengzi but was secretly saved by his senior sect brother, Dao Xuan. He spent the rest of his life guarding the Ancestral Hall. Ultimately, during a confrontation with Zhang Xiaofan, he was fatally ambushed by Ghost Sir and died, leaving Dao Xuan heartbroken. Dao Xuan insisted on placing his memorial tablet in the Ancestral Hall. Later, Wan Jianyi's spirit appeared in the Illusory Moon Cave to enlighten Dao Xuan and handed the Zhu Xian Sword to Zhang Xiaofan, enabling him to eradicate the Demon Sect."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/WanJianyi-749b16.png"},"Wen Min":{"title":"Wen Min","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"文敏","species":["Human"],"gender":"Female","aliases":["Min'er"],"masters":["⟦Shui Yue|Shui Yue⟧"],"spouse":["⟦Song Daren|Song Daren⟧"],"continent":["Shenzou"],"region":["Central Plain"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Wen Min (文敏) is a female character in the novels Zhu Xian and Zhu Xian II."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Together with ⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧, they were known as the \"Twin Beauties of Xiaozhu Peak\". In the novel, she is described as having \"hair like clouds, skin as white as snow, with a faint smile hanging at the corner of her mouth.\""},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Elegant, gentle, serene, and wise."},{"t":"p","x":"This is likely the meaning behind the name \"Wen Min\"."},{"t":"p","x":"Therefore, her story is characterized by a gentle and serene warmth, without the dramatic ups and downs experienced by her junior sister Lu Xueqi."},{"t":"p","x":"However, her understanding and considerate, gentle nature leave a deep impression."},{"t":"p","x":"Towards her Master Shuiyue , she is filial and understanding; towards her junior sister Xueqi, she is attentive and caring; towards Song Daren , she is deeply devoted."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She is the eldest disciple under Master Shuiyue, the head of Xiaozhu Peak of the Qingyun Sect . She is the senior sister of Lu Xueqi and is as close as sisters with her, and she is deeply in love with Song Daren , a disciple of Dazhu Peak."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Wen Min first met Song Daren during the Seven Peaks Tournament. They eventually became a couple after enduring the trials of the Righteous-Demonic War. As the head disciple of Xiaozhu Peak, she maintained the relationship between the two peaks with her gentle and graceful temperament."},{"t":"p","x":"In the end, after Song Daren succeeded as the head of Dazhu Peak, Wen Min married him, becoming one of the characters in the book whose romantic storyline reaches a happy conclusion."}],"ep":6,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive","Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Wenmings4-da0172.webp"},"Xiao Bai":{"title":"Xiao Bai","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"小白","species":["Nine Tailed Fox"],"gender":"Female","spouse":["(Unknown)"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Bai is a character in the novels Zhu Xian and Zhu Xian II. Having cultivated for a thousand years, she possesses profound cultivation and divine magical powers."},{"t":"h","x":"Xiao Bai side character of Zhu Xian (Jade Dynasty).","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Bai just like big sister for Zhang Xiao Fan and Lu Xueqi."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She has a peerless beauty, on par with the heroine Lu Xueqi. One is celestial and the other is charming, and they are equally matched."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She possesses a passionate and unrestrained personality, enjoying a carefree and playful life."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Because she stole the artifact Xuanhuojian, she was imprisoned for three hundred years by the ancient \" Eight Evil Xuanhuo Formation \" on the highest level of the Xuanhuo Altar, a forbidden area in Fenxiang Valley . Later, by chance, she was rescued by the hero Zhang Xiaofan (Ghost Li). Because she had not used her original name for so long, she was named \"Xiaobai\" after the white fox."},{"t":"p","x":"She was grateful and helped Zhang Xiaofan many times.In Zhu Xian II , Xiaobai discovers the descendants of the Sky Fox clan and asks Zhang Xiaofan to help revive the Sky Fox clan"},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She is the nine-tailed celestial fox with the highest level of Taoism in the ancient celestial fox clan , and the most intelligent and mysterious branch of the fox demon clan."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Xiao Liu","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Liu,the six-tailed spirit fox, is Xiao Bai's son."}],"ep":42,"ch":114,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/小白_𝑿𝒊𝒂𝒐_𝑩𝒂𝒊__1-3fb51b.jpg","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/小白_𝑿𝒊𝒂𝒐_𝑩𝒂𝒊-52830b.jpg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/小白_𝑿𝒊𝒂𝒐_𝑩𝒂𝒊__2-f8d79b.jpg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/小白_𝑿𝒊𝒂𝒐_𝑩𝒂𝒊_3-073d43.jpg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/小白_𝑿𝒊𝒂𝒐_𝑩𝒂𝒊_桂莉_𝑮𝒖𝒊_𝑳𝒊_Z𝒉𝑎𝑛𝑔_𝑋𝑖𝑎𝑜𝑓𝑎𝑛-f74e6e.jpg","cap":""}]},"Xiao Chi":{"title":"Xiao Chi","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"小痴","gender":"Female","spouse":["⟦Ghost King|Ghost King⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Chi ( 小痴 ) is a character in the novel Jade Dynasty. She is the wife of the ⟦Ghost King|Ghost King⟧ , the leader of the Demon Sect's Ghost King Sect, and the mother of ⟦Bi Yao|Bi Yao⟧."},{"t":"p","x":"Her true form is the younger sister of the Nine-tailed Heavenly Fox, ⟦Xiao Bai|Xiao Bai⟧ . Her life story is presented through the recollections of others, and she never makes a formal appearance in the works. She has a connection to the Ghost King Sect spanning centuries, and the fox tribe she belongs to has long resided on Huqi Mountain."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[]},"Xiao Huan":{"title":"Xiao Huan","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Female"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Huan is a female character in Zhu Xian and its sequel, Zhu Xian II."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Huan is lovely and beautiful, innocent and lively, always treating everyone with the utmost kindness."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Traveling the martial world as a fortune teller, Xiao Huan is inherently kind-hearted and fond of eating candied haws on a stick. She once used the Soul Retrieval Art to save Jin Ping'er at the cost of one year of her lifespan, and later expended over twenty years of her lifespan to rescue ⟦Ye Gou|Ye Gou⟧ Daoren (Taoist Ye Gou). During these rescues, she laid down a blood array and used her own blood to perform the art. Although she developed feelings for the male protagonist Zhang Xiaofan, her affection was not reciprocated."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Nüwa Reincarnation."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Adopted by Zhou Yixian since childhood, she first appeared at the age of eight, displaying a talent in physiognomy. At eighteen, she inherited the secret arts of the Ghost Path, possessing the magical treasures Blood Jade Bone Fragments and the Soul Extinguishing Tower, gifts from Ghost Master . After cultivating the Ghost Path Art for merely one month, she was barely able to withstand ⟦Dao Xuan|Dao Xuan⟧."},{"t":"p","x":"She is proficient in physiognomy and possesses a rare talent not seen in a century in the ghostly arts. To save Jin Ping'er and Taoist ⟦Ye Gou|Ye Gou⟧, she did not hesitate to use the Soul Retrieval Art, shortening her own lifespan. She became sworn sisters with Jin Ping'er of the Demon Sect and shared a subtle emotional bond with Ye Gou Daoren."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/XiaoHuanS2-a2fab5.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao_huan_2x2-070222.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao_Huan_2x2_sentada-b8295c.png","cap":""}]},"Xiao Hui":{"title":"Xiao Hui","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"小灰","species":["Spiritual Beast"],"aliases":["Little Grey"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xiaohui (Little Grey, 小灰) is a Three-Eyed Spiritual Monkey by nature, he appears in works such as Jade Dynasty, Jade Dynasty II, and Lu Xian, serving as the long-time spiritual beast of the protagonist, ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ (Guili). His spiritual nature is reflected in his ability to sense the spiritual energy of heaven and earth, his love for strong liquor, and his close interactions with other exotic beasts like ⟦Dahuang|Dahuang⟧ and ⟦Taotie|Taotie⟧."},{"t":"p","x":"First encountering Zhang Xiaofan at Big Bamboo Peak on Mount Qingyun, he remains by the protagonist's side through the conflicts between good and evil. Mischievous yet fiercely loyal, he never abandoned Zhang Xiaofan even when he fell into the demonic realm, and during battle, he can awaken into a formidable Three-Eyed Fiend Monkey form. In his daily life, he loves playing pranks and fooling around; he once mistook a painting of a crouching tiger in a thicket for a portrait of Dahuang and insisted on taking it, and he formed a friendship with the Taotie by bribing it with food, showcasing his unique wit. After consuming the Immortal Elixir and the Nether Stone of Heaven and Earth, his potential was unlocked prematurely, allowing him to open his third spiritual eye during the Battle of Incense Valley and evolve into a giant beast."},{"t":"p","x":"As a core spiritual beast spanning the series, Xiaohui grows from an intelligent, cute pet into a pivotal battle force. He serves not only as Zhang Xiaofan’s emotional anchor but also as a key thread driving the plot forward. His abilities encompass farsighted vision (Clairvoyance) and Five Elements Immortal Arts, eventually granting him the power of immortality."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/Xiaohui-434410.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao_hui_3-2113f0.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao_hui_IoI-c320f0.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao_hui_2-9bb901.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao_hui_1-59ece5.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao_Hui_XD-ff37bc.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Xioa_hui_rsrs-72eb0d.png","cap":""}]},"Xiao Liu":{"title":"Xiao Liu","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"小六","species":["Six Tailed Demon Fox"],"gender":"Male","spouse":["⟦Xiao Mei|Xiao Mei⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Liu, also known as the Six-Tailed White Fox, is a character in the novel Jade Dynasty and its derivative works."},{"t":"p","x":"He is a Six-Tailed Spirit Fox of the Heavenly Fox Lineage, whose former residence was located at Huqi Mountain in the Southern Border."},{"t":"p","x":"His mother, the Nine-Tailed Heavenly Fox ⟦Xiao Bai|Xiao Bai⟧ , was imprisoned for three hundred years in the Mystical Fire Altar for stealing the Mystical Fire Mirror, a treasure of the Burning Incense Valley."},{"t":"p","x":"This resulted in Xiao Liu losing his protector from a young age. Afflicted by the Burning Incense Valley's secret technique, the Nine Cold Ice Thorns, Xiao Liu suffered from invasive ice poison and the destruction of his cultivation foundation. He ultimately committed suicide with his lover, the Three-Tailed Demon Fox, in the magma of the Black Stone Cave. Before his death, he entrusted the Mystical Fire Mirror to Zhang Xiaofan ."},{"t":"p","x":"As a descendant of the Heavenly Fox, Xiao Liu belonged to a fox clan whose cultivation realms were distinguished by the number of tails. His tragic fate is closely linked to the calamity that befell his clan, which was triggered by his mother's theft of the treasure."},{"t":"p","x":"This character appears during the Fox Calamity Incident at Black Stone Cave in Small Pond Town. Although his appearance is brief, his entangled background and life-and-death choices reveal the emotional dimension of the demon race."}],"ep":16,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Xiao_Liu-c1273d.webp"},"Xiao Mei":{"title":"Xiao Mei","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Three Tailed Demon Fox"],"gender":"Female","spouse":["⟦Xiao Liu|Xiao Liu⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Mei is a character in the story of the novel Zhu Xian. She is a three-tailed demon fox who is over 300 years old. Xiao Liu once saved her, and since then, Xiao Mei has followed him."},{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Mei is the name used for the character in the donghua adaptation, while in the novel and live-action drama, she is simply referred to as the Three-Tailed Fox."}],"ep":15,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Xiao_Mei-6f06fb.webp"},"Xiao Yicai":{"title":"Xiao Yicai","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Male","aliases":["萧逸才 (Xiao Yicai)"],"masters":["⟦Dao Xuan|Dao Xuan⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Yicai (萧逸才) is a male character in the novel Zhu Xian and its sequel Zhu Xian II."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Xiao Yicai possesses a slender build and handsome appearance, with sharp eyebrows and bright eyes, he wields the magical artifact Seven Star Sword, and has mastered the Tai Chi Xuan Qing Dao."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"His personality is calm, resourceful, and profound. He demonstrated decisiveness in consolidating Qingyun's forces and opposing the Demon Sect. He is Intelligent and steady, courageous and resourceful, deep and calculating, ambitious and strategic."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"As the personal disciple of Qingyun Sect's leader Daoxuan Zhenren, Xiao Yicai won the championship in the 19th Seven Meridians Tournament, establishing himself as a leading figure among the younger generation of the Qingyun Sect."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"In his early years, under his master's orders, he infiltrated the Demon Sect's Lianxue Hall as a spy. His identity was exposed during the Liubo Mountain Incident, after which he broke through the encirclement alongside Tian Ling'er and Zhang Xiaofan."},{"t":"p","x":"Following Daoxuan Zhenren's disappearance, he acted as the proxy administrator of Qingyun affairs, later succeeding as sect leader."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/XiaoYicaiS2-c17ccf.png"},"Xuanwu":{"title":"Xuanwu","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"玄武","gender":"Male","aliases":["Xuan Wu","Black Tortoise"],"masters":["Ghost King"],"occupation":["One of the 4 Holy Envoys of the Ghost King sect"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Xuan Wu (玄武, literally Black Tortoise) is a character in the novel Jade Dynasty (Zhu Xian). he was formerly a subordinate of ⟦Chou Wangyu|Chou Wangyu⟧. He is ranked fourth of the Ghost King Sect's Four Holy Envoys."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Xuanwu-1e7309.webp"},"Yan Hong":{"title":"Yan Hong","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Female","aliases":["燕虹"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Yan Hong is a female character in the novel Jade Dynasty. She is a disciple of ⟦Yun Yi Lan|Yun Yilan⟧, the master of Burning Incense Valley, and the junior sister of ⟦Li Xun|Li Xun⟧. Together, they are known as the \"Two Outstanding Disciples of Burning Incense Valley.\""},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Her face is as lovely as a lotus flower, exuding delicate and soft beauty."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Her personality is low-key, calm, and thoughtful."},{"t":"p","x":"Despite belonging to a prestigious sect, she maintains a humble nature, showing great respect to her elders and teachers, and cooperating seamlessly with her fellow disciples. Her gentle and reserved temperament contrasts with the arrogant style of Burning Incense Valley, as she consistently fulfills her righteous mission with an uncontentious demeanor."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She wields the magical treasure Green Spirit Stone and cultivates the Burning Incense Jade Book technique."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"As a righteous disciple of Burning Incense Valley, Yan Hong participates in major events such as the Kongsang Mountain Training. While investigating the Mystic Fire Mirror in the Fire Dragon Cave, she demonstrates keen insight. In the Inner Dead Marsh, she cooperates with Xiao Yicai to confront Jin Ping'er of the Demon Sect, showcasing her cautious approach to handling affairs."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/YanHong-9327a8.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Who_is_she-11f840.png","cap":""}]},"Ye Gou":{"title":"Ye Gou","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"野狗道人","gender":"Male","aliases":["Ye Gou Daoren"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Ye Gou (野狗道人, literally Wild Dog) is a character in the novels Zhu Xian and Zhu Xian II . He was a member of the Blood Refining Guild, and ends up following ⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ in season 2, and later, he followed ⟦Xiao Huan|Xiao Huan⟧ and ⟦Zhou Yi Xian|Zhou Yixian⟧ to wander the world in season 3 and 4."},{"t":"p","x":"His friends usually call him Ye Gou Dao Ren (Taoist Ye Gou)."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"His distinctive features include drooping eyelids and lips as crimson as a dog's."},{"t":"p","x":"He was described as quite tall in stature, but with an extremely peculiar appearance: drooping eyelids, a prominent nose, ears that pointed upward, crimson lips, and an apparently rather long tongue that frequently darted out of his mouth, making him look very much like a dog."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Originally an orphan before he was picked up by the Blood-Refining Guild, has a foul mouth but a kind heart."},{"t":"p","x":"Although he bullies the weak and fears the strong, a trace of self-awareness of being a \"bad person\" in his heart adds some \"color\" to the character. He is concerned about face and likes to have the last word in the moment. In fact, he is kind-hearted and has always silently admired Xiao Huan."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is a member of the Blood Refining Guild, and his weapon is the Tusk Club. Abandoned by his parents due to his strange appearance, he was raised by wild dogs."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He was the only member of the Blood Refining Hall who would rather die than surrender during its downfall, and his loyalty moved Gui Li to take him under his wing."},{"t":"p","x":"Later, he followed Xiao Huan and Zhou Yixian to wander the world."},{"t":"p","x":"During the Beast Demon War, he shielded Xiao Huan from a demon beast with his own body. Mortally wounded and on the verge of death, he was revived by Xiao Huan using the Soul Collecting Technique."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Xiao Huan","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"After giving an umbrella to Xiao Huan in the Dead Marsh, he developed hidden feelings for her, and ultimately followed Xiao Huan and Zhou Yixian to wander the world."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/Yegous2-a15421.webp","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Yegou_2x2-7a5820.png","cap":""}]},"You Ji":{"title":"You Ji","kind":"character","facts":{"gender":"Female","aliases":["幽姬","You Yi","Vermilion Bird","Zhu Que (朱雀)"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"You Ji (幽姬) is a female character in the novel Zhu Xian and its prequel ⟦Savage Journey (Prequel Novel)|Savage Journey⟧."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She is clad in black robes, veils her face with a light gauze, possesses peerless beauty, and is enigmatic and inscrutable, with profound cultivation."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"She is meticulous and kind-hearted. She once had a vague and ambiguous affection for Wan Jianyi."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"As one of the Four Holy Envoys of the Ghost King Sect, she holds the title \"Vermilion Bird.\" She is the only woman among the Four Holy Envoys and ranks third."},{"t":"p","x":"She holds a pivotal position within the Ghost King Sect and is very close to the Ghost King's daughter, Bi Yao , who affectionately calls her \"Aunt You.\""},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Over a hundred years ago, she encountered Wan Jianyi of the righteous Qingyun Sect. Though their meeting took place in the midst of battle, it left a lasting impression on You Ji, causing her to fall deeply in love with Wan Jianyi and making him impossible for her to forget."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Martial Brothers","l":3},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Senior brothers: Qing Long , Bai Hu"],[1,"Junior brother: Xuan Wu"]]},{"t":"p","x":"Note: Four of them are known as the Four Holy Envoys of the Ghost King Sect."},{"t":"h","x":"Bi Yao","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"After the death of Bi Yao's mother, Xiao Chi , You Ji provided her with maternal love and is called \"Aunt You\" by Bi Yao."}],"ep":9,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/YouYi-5627c6.png"},"Yu Du City":{"title":"Yu Du City","kind":"place","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Yu Du City (渝都城, Yūdū Chéng), also sometimes called \"River City\", is a wealthy, independent trading port city-state governed by the Shangguan family, which prioritizes commerce, stability, and neutrality above the sect conflicts between the orthodox and demonic paths. It serves as a crucial neutral ground where cultivators from opposing factions can temporarily coexist under its rule of law, though its neutrality is often tested by external conspiracies and internal power struggles that threaten its peace."},{"t":"p","x":"Zeng Shushu is the grandson of the City Lord, Shangguan Ce."}]},"Yun Yi Lan":{"title":"Yun Yi Lan","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Yun Yilan is a character in the novel Zhu Xian. He is the master of the Fen Xiang Valley, one of the three major sects of the Central Plains' Righteous Path, and the teacher of Li Xun."},{"t":"p","x":"He cultivated his sect's supreme cultivation method, the Burning Incense Jade Tome, to the Jade Yang Realm, a feat unprecedented in the 800-year history of Fen Xiang Valley. Although he possesses profound cultivation, his prestige and strength are far inferior to Qingyun Sect's leader Dao Xuan."}],"ep":54,"ch":null,"tags":["Human"],"img":"img/wiki/Yun_Yilan-0a6549.jpg"},"Zeng Shucang":{"title":"Zeng Shucang","kind":"character","facts":{"titles":["Head of Wind Blowing Peak"]},"blocks":[],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Zengshucang-66e6b8.png"},"Zeng Shushu":{"title":"Zeng Shushu","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"曾书书","gender":"Male","masters":["⟦Zheng Shucang|Zheng Shucang⟧"]},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Zeng Shushu is a character in the novel Jade Dynasty and its sequel, Jade Dynasty II. Originally named Zeng Yingxiong, One of Zhang Xiaofan's friends from Qingyun Sect. Loves to tinker with contraptions instead of cultivating."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Delicate facial features, dressed in a long robe, around twenty years old, with a pair of large, bright eyes."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He has a humorous and lively personality, is knowledgeable and has a strong memory, and enjoys collecting rare and exotic beasts."},{"t":"p","x":"Carefree, but is very loyal to his friend, tries to maintain a friendship with Zhang Xiaofan after he joins the Ghost sect. He is very interested in different monsters. When he first met Xiaofan Zheng Shishu begged him to give ⟦Xiao Hui|Xiao Hui⟧ to him."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is the only son of ⟦Zeng Shuchang|Zeng Shuchang⟧ (the head of Feng Hui Peak of the Qingyun Sect ). Because he loved reading from a young age, his father renamed him 'Shushu'. As a nineteenth-generation disciple of the Qingyun Sect and the most outstanding representative of the younger generation of Feng Hui Peak, Zeng Shushu is exceptionally talented."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He entered the top four as a favorite in the Twentieth Seven Meridians Tournament, wielding the treasure Xuanyuan Sword."}],"ep":null,"ch":null,"tags":["Alive"],"img":"img/wiki/ZengShushuS2-bb3d7d.png","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Zeng_Shushu_formation-92e122.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Zeng_Shushu_2-70b6d2.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Zen_Shushu_3-747322.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Zen_Shushu_4-16316b.png","cap":""}]},"Zhang Xiaoding":{"title":"Zhang Xiaoding","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"\"I want to be with my father and mother for the rest of my life.\"","l":5},{"t":"p","x":"- Zhang Xiao DingZhang Xiaoding is one of the main characters in the Xianxia novel \"Zhu Xian II \". Xiao Ding is smart, talented, cute, lively, strong and sensible. He is the beloved son of Zhang Xiaofan, the mysterious chef of Dazhu Peak, and Lu Xueqi, one of the five elders of Qingyun Sect. Suspected to be the legendary figure from \" Slaughter of the Immortals \" - Yuan Wentian. Yuan Wentian often comes to a bamboo house in a bamboo forest . On the wall, an ordinary man in coarse linen and a woman in white sit hand in hand, smiling."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Short hair , round face, round hands, round feet and round belly, a magic blue cloud bag hanging on his waist, and big eyes that are full of spirit."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Alert and smart, naughty, lively, cute, enthusiastic, calm, domineering, strong, and sensible."},{"t":"h","x":"Relationship","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"⟦Zhang Xiaofan|Zhang Xiaofan⟧ (Father) ⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧ (Mother) ⟦Qi Xiaoxuan|Qi Xiaoxuan⟧ (Wife)"},{"t":"h","x":"Magic Weapon","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"Liuyun Bag (a palm-sized treasure-protecting bag made by Zhang Xiaofan himself. It contains countless rare treasures. Food can be kept fresh and warm. When in danger, a blue light will automatically pop up, and his mother will rush to rescue him in time.)"],[1,"Fart Funnel ( Made by Zhang Xiaofan and named by Xiaoding, it is a chili water made from the large red peppers that are a specialty of Dazhu Peak . It is sprayed by squeezing the air sac. It is harmful but not fatal.) (Excerpt from the original text: Then Xiao Ding laughed and said, \"This thing doesn't have a name, but every time I use it, it feels like farting, so I call it a 'fart funnel.')"],[1,"Fragment of the Ancient Sword of Killing Immortals (from \" Killing Immortals \", suspected to have a connection with the Ancient Sword of Killing Immortals)"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"From birth to the age of three, his father used the True Method to strengthen his meridians and energy channels daily, making his physique far superior to that of an ordinary child."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is a disciple of Qingyun Mountain and lives in the Wood Room of the 23rd Courtyard of the B Dao of Qingyun Villa at the foot of Qingyun Mountain. He returns to Dazhu Peak every seven days. He went on many adventures with the protagonist Wang Zongjing , and inadvertently paved the way for Wang Zongjing to meet Zhang Xiaofan.Later, every time he returned to Dazhu Peak, he would bring Wang Zongjing with him to see Zhang Xiaofan. He and Wang Zongjing had adventures in strange places and their friendship grew deep.\"I know I wasn't a good kid. I did a lot of bad things. I threw rocks into the hot soup my father had made . I splashed ink on my mother's favorite white dress. I said Aunt Wen looked thin but was actually full of flesh. I told ghost stories that scared Xiaoxuan so much she cried. I tore up the books of several of my senior teachers, set fire to their houses, urinated on them, and even stole Dahuang's bones, chewed the meat, and threw them down the mountain so he wouldn't eat them.\""}],"img":"img/wiki/Xiaoding_s_most_love-7b18ef.jpg","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Zhang_Xiao_Ding-8ecf7b.jpg","cap":""}]},"Zhang Xiaofan":{"title":"Zhang Xiaofan","kind":"character","facts":{"zh":"张小凡","species":["Human"],"gender":"Male","titles":["Blood Prince (Xue Gongzi / 血公子)"],"aliases":["Gui Li (鬼厉)","Ghost Li","Blood Demon"],"masters":["⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Buyi⟧ (former) ⟦Puzhi|Puzhi⟧ (temporary)"],"spouse":["⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧"],"occupation":["Deputy Leader of Ghost King sect"]},"blocks":[{"t":"quote","x":"Why are you so nice to me?","by":""},{"t":"quote","x":"I can no longer go back","by":""},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan (mandarin: 张小凡) is the main protagonist in Zhu Xian (Jade Dynasty)."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is of ordinary appearance."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Determined, loyal and brave. Appears to be slow-witted but is actually very intelligent."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan came from humble beginnings, born in a rural village, Caomiao Village, that was located near Qingyun Sect."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"One day, in the rural village, he and his friend, ⟦Lin Jingyu|Lin Jingyu⟧ were having another spar to see who would win and they ran into a monk, Master Puzhi who was resting at a run-down temple in the village."},{"t":"p","x":"That night, Master Puzhi was fighting against someone who desperately wanted the sinister bead in the monk's possession. Everyone in the village was also killed as a result, leaving Zhang Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu as the survivors."},{"t":"p","x":"Master Puzhi was also seriously injured and Zhang Xiaofan happened to come across him."},{"t":"p","x":"Since Master Puzhi had no one else he could rely on, he chose Zhang Xiaofan to take care of the sinister bead in his possession, telling him to throw it away somewhere once he finds a safe place to do so. In return, he passed on some cultivation techniques to him."},{"t":"p","x":"But he warned him to never reveal his name to outsiders for his own safety."},{"t":"p","x":"A few days later, cultivators from Qingyun Sect stopped by and saw the tragedy and took in Zhang Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu. Zhang Xiaofan ended up going to the Da Zhu (Big Bamboo) Peak of Qingyun Sect because no one else wanted to take in a mediocre apprentice."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan works incredibly hard over the years, trying his best to cultivate with the techniques that his Shifu passed on to him but what he didn't realize was that the buddhist techniques passed on to him from the monk interfered with his progress with the dao techniques of Qingyun Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"One day he acquires a soul-sucking club that fused with the sinister bead in his possession when he was training in the mountains. The fusion of these two items improves his cultivation but the items are demonic in nature.After the items fuse, it was almost time for the internal martial arts competition within the sect. But no one expects him to get far within the competition. Not his master, his senior sister or his fellow senior brothers."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan wins his first match when his blood drips onto his artifact and triggers an explosive amount of power."},{"t":"p","x":"He ends up being in the top 4 after the martial arts competition ends and goes down the mountain to meet up with the other 3 to investigate the Bat Cave in Mt. Kongshang. Rumors say there might be demonic sects involved."},{"t":"p","x":"At this point, some of the leaders of the other peaks within Qingyun Sect are suspicious of the staff artifact in Zhang Xiaofan's possession."},{"t":"p","x":"When he and the other cultivators: ⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧, ⟦Zeng Shushu|Zeng Shushu⟧, ⟦Qi Hao|Qi Hao⟧ descend down the mountain to the nearby town, Zhang Xiaofan meets ⟦Bi Yao|Bi Yao⟧ for the first time in a restaurant while Zeng Shushu orders some delicious dishes for them. Their group decides to rest for a night before continuing on their journey."},{"t":"p","x":"At night, he encounters her again when he wakes up from a terrifying nightmare of bloody hands trying to pull him into the depths."},{"t":"p","x":"He asked her why she plucked a flower when she was perfectly capable of admiring it without touching it. In response she said, \"it's this flower's blessing that I reached out to pluck it.\" This was the beginning of Bi Yao's friendship with Zhang Xiaofan."},{"t":"p","x":"After a brief encounter with Bi Yao, Zhang Xiaofan and his group continue towards the Bat Cave at Mt. Kongshang. His group meets up with other righteous sect members and he exchanges blows with ⟦Ye Gou|Ye Gou⟧ from the ⟦Sects|Blood-Refining Sect⟧."},{"t":"p","x":"More members of the Blood-Refining Sect show up including one of the elders, ⟦Nian Lao Da|Nian Lao Da⟧ and Zhang Xiaofan and his group are pushed to their limits. As a desperate move, he volunteers to buy his group some time while he holds the members of the Blood-Refining Sect off."},{"t":"p","x":"The Sect Leader clashes blows with Zhang Xiaofan and the explosion pushes Zhang Xiaofan off a cliff within the cave. Lu Xueqi tries to save him but ends up going down with him."},{"t":"p","x":"It turned out to be a secret area within the Bat Cave and there were a lot of evil spirits lurking about. While Zhang Xiaofan was unconscious, large amounts of evil spirits got sucked into his demonic artifact while Lu Xueqi had her spiritual energy sucked away."},{"t":"p","x":"When he finally regained consciousness, there was a demonic tree-like creature that was siphoning off Lu Xueqi's energy. Zhang Xiaofan broke out of his restraints and defeated the creature."},{"t":"p","x":"After the creature is defeated, Zhang Xiaofan meets Bi Yao again who had her own plans for the Blood-Refining Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"But that's not the only creature in this special area. A massive serpent like creature wakes up and splits up Zhang Xiaofan and Lu Xueqi because Lu Xueqi is too weakened to fight. Lu Xueqi ends up meeting back with their original group and she is forced to retreat."},{"t":"p","x":"While Zhang Xiaofan ends up with Bi Yao and they find a hidden cove that is called the Blood-Soaked Cove. Inside this cove, there is the skeleton remains of an old ancestor named Heixin Lao Ren who was affiliated with Bi Yao's Ghost King Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"The two venture deeper into the cove because there's no other way out and find statues that suggest this was the original headquarters of the Blood-Refining Hall."},{"t":"p","x":"It was also here that Zhang Xiaofan notices some techniques written on the walls that resemble those from Buddhist and Taoism techniques. He was extremely confused to see techniques that resembled those of the righteous sects here since this was suppose to be the headquarters of the demonic sect."},{"t":"p","x":"After Bi Yao pays her respects to the statues and slices her hand for some blood and then places the Happy Reunion Bell she picked up earlier in the same area onto the ground behind the statues, it triggers something and the two of them are finally able to leave."},{"t":"p","x":"Once the two of them are out, Zhang Xiaofan acknowledges Bi Yao as his friend since the two of them survived and avoided death from being trapped in the underground cave."},{"t":"p","x":"He also realizes that even though she is from one of the demonic sect, she's not that much different from him after all."},{"t":"p","x":"After they go their separate ways, he continues his journey in order to reunite with his sect members and encounters the Ghost King who recognizes his artifacts."},{"t":"p","x":"Even though he becomes aware of its demonic origins, he plans to continue using it to fight evil."},{"t":"h","x":"Quotes","l":2},{"t":"quote","x":"Why are you so nice to me?","by":""},{"t":"quote","x":"I can no longer go back","by":""},{"t":"h","x":"Relationships","l":2},{"t":"h","x":"Lu Xueqi","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"She is the wife and love of Zhang Xiaofan."},{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan continues to win in the internal martial arts competition within the Qingyun Sect until he eventually becomes matched up with ⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧. No one expects him to win against Lu Xueqi because she is considered one of the best cultivators within the sect. When the fight starts Zhang Xiaofan is distracted and dissapointed that his senior sister Tian Ling'er whom he had crush on wasn't there to watch him."},{"t":"p","x":"This makes Lu Xueqi dominate the fight for the most time and after sometime Xiaofan gets serious and attackers her seriously while now in dominant position .However, just when he is about to win (due to the overwhelming effect of his artifacts), he gives up the match when he sees Lu Xueqi as his Senior Sister, Tian Ling'er. Lu Xueqi was badly injured but still uses Mighty Sword of Thunder even though her cultivation wasn't enough for it to be performed which worsens her injury even more. Zhang Xiaofan then takes the last blow without attacking her from his orb stick."},{"t":"p","x":"Thinking that Zhang Xiaofan intentionally gave up the attack she asks him the reason to which he replies that its fault from his side so ⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧ shouldn't think that he gave her the easy way. While thinking about it her icy heart gets melted due to which she slowly develops feelings for him without knowing."},{"t":"p","x":"When their group is attacked by people from Blood Refining Sect Zhang Xiaofan and Lu Xueqi protect each other. When the Sect Leader of Blood Refining Sect kicks Zhang Xiaofan from the cliff, she also jumps with him without any hesitation. When Zhang Xiaofan was accused of being a spy from Demon Cult and was arrested then also she steps out and gives grantee on her life that he could never collude with demons."},{"t":"p","x":"After ten years she has completely fallen in love with him even though she knows they both can't be together because of their different paths. She even rejects the marriage proposal and disobeys her master ⟦Shui Yue|Shui Yue⟧ for the first time because she can't make space for another man in her heart other than Xiaofan."},{"t":"p","x":"Everyone on Small Bamboo Peak including her master knows that she already has Zhang Xiaofan in her heart but can't refuse the marriage proposal as its a way to unite all Sects."},{"t":"h","x":"Bi Yao","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"When he initially met her, his initial impression was that she was a witch since she belonged to one of the demonic cultivation sects. However, through countless of interactions and life-and-death situations with her, he realized that she was just another human being, just like him. Like him, she had her own traumas and her own sad past and she could relate to him. They became friends despite coming from cultivation backgrounds that should make them mortal enemies."},{"t":"p","x":"Moreover, she believed in him and thought he had potential even though everyone thought he wouldn't amount to anything. When she blocked the ultimate sword technique for him while he was trying to leave the Qingyun Sect for good, she sacrificed her soul to do so and he felt incredibly guilty."},{"t":"p","x":"Because he still owed her an answer to her question... he didn't get a chance to tell her... that he was the one who saw her in that deep, dark cave that day. That he was the one who threw the buns down to her..."},{"t":"h","x":"Lin Jingyu","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"His childhood friend from the same village, Caomiao Village and a rival that he looks up to. After the tragedy in the village, he was the only person left that was close to him, almost like a real brother. When they both joined Qingyun Sect and got split up due to their inherent potential, Zhang Xiaofan thought it be great if his skills could reach up to Lin Jingyu's level one day."},{"t":"p","x":"He was the only other person who thought he could amount to something as well."},{"t":"h","x":"Tian Buyi","l":3},{"t":"p","x":"His master from Qingyun Sect and head of the Big Bamboo Peak. Even though his master reluctantly took him in, Zhang Xiaofan always wanted to be someone his master could be proud of. Zhang Xiaofan worked hard to gain his recognition even though the conflicting cultivation methods in his body made it tough for him to level up his skills. Almost a father-like figure for Zhang Xiaofan as well."}],"ep":1,"ch":1,"tags":["Alive","Human"],"tabs":[{"name":"Cultivation","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Zhang Xiaofan learned and combined cultivation from three paths: Buddhism, Taoism, and the Demonic path."},{"t":"table","rows":[["1.","Mortal Realm",""],["2.","Earthly Realm",""],["3.","Heavenly Realm",""],["4.","Divine Realm",""],["5.","Immortal Realm",""],["6.","Sage Realm",""],["7.","Saint Realm",""],["8.","God Realm",""]]}]},{"name":"Items","blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Weapon","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Sinister Bead|Sinister Bead⟧"],[1,"Soul-sucking Club (fused with the sinister bead)"],[1,"Xuanhuo Mirror (Mystic Fire Mirror)"]]}]},{"name":"Quotes","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"如果这一切注定会失去，我还愿不愿开始？"},{"t":"p","x":"Rúguǒ zhè yīqiè zhùdìng huì shīqù, wǒ hái yuàn bù yuàn kāishǐ?"},{"t":"p","x":"\"Jika semua ini ditakdirkan untuk hilang, apakah aku masih rela memulainya?\""}]},{"name":"Relationship","blocks":[{"t":"h","x":"Wife","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Love Interest","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Tian Ling'er|Tian Ling'er⟧ (First Love)"],[1,"⟦Lu Xueqi|Lu Xueqi⟧"],[1,"⟦Bi Yao|Bi Yao⟧"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Children","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Zhang Xiaoding|Zhang XiaoDing⟧"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Relatives","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Bu Yi⟧ (Teacher)"],[1,"⟦Su Ru|Su Ru⟧ (Teacher's Wife)"],[1,"⟦Tian Ling'er|Tian Linger⟧ (Teacher's daughter)"],[1,"⟦Dao Xuan|Taoist Master Dao Xuan⟧ (Head of Tongtian Peak)"],[1,"⟦Cang Song|Taoist Cang Song⟧ (Head of Longshou Peak)"],[1,"⟦Shui Yue|Master Shui Yue⟧ (Head of Xiaozhu Peak)"],[1,"⟦Shang Zhengliang|Shang Zheliang⟧ (Head of Chaoyang Peak)"],[1,"⟦Qi Hao|Qi Hao⟧ (His brother in law)"],[1,"Qi Xiao Xuan (His niece)"],[1,"⟦Wen Min|Wen Min⟧ (His sister in law)"],[1,"⟦Wan Jianyi|Wan Jia Yi⟧ (His senior)"],[1,"⟦Song Daren|Song Daren⟧ (His senior)"],[1,"⟦Xiao Yicai|Xiao Yicai⟧ (His Senior)"],[1,"Wang Dayi (His senior)"],[1,"Zheng Dali (His senior)"],[1,"Dia Dazhi (His senior)"],[1,"Lu Daxin (His senior)"],[1,"Du Bishu (His senior)"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Friends","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Xiao Hui|Xiao Hui⟧"],[1,"Da Huang"],[1,"⟦Lin Jingyu|Lin Jing Yu⟧"],[1,"⟦Zeng Shushu|Zheng Shu Shu⟧"],[1,"⟦Zhou Yi Xian|Zhou Yi Xian⟧"],[1,"⟦Xiao Huan|Zhou Xiao Huan⟧"],[1,"⟦Xiao Bai|Xiao Bai⟧"],[1,"⟦Bi Yao|Bi Yao⟧"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Allies","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Jin Ping'er|Jin Pinger⟧"],[1,"⟦Qin Wuyan|Qin Wuyan⟧"],[1,"⟦Ye Gou|Ye Gou⟧"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Masters","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Master Puzhi|Pu Zhi⟧"],[1,"⟦Tian Buyi|Tian Bu Yi⟧"]]},{"t":"h","x":"Rivals","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"⟦Li Xun|Li Xun⟧ (Love rivals)"},{"t":"h","x":"Enemies","l":2},{"t":"ul","items":[[1,"⟦Beast Deity|Beast Deity⟧"],[1,"⟦Ghost King|Ghost King⟧"]]}]},{"name":"Techniques","blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"He mastered and fused cultivation techniques from three schools: Buddhism, Taoism, and Demonic. The demonic techniques were learned from various volumes of the Heavenly Books and from the Ghost King after he joined the Ghost King Sect."}]}],"img":"img/wiki/Zhang_Xiaofan-4ea909.jpg","gallery":[{"src":"img/wiki/Manhua-0e7b94.jpg","cap":"Manhua"},{"src":"img/wiki/Z-fe286f.png","cap":"Donghua Season 2"},{"src":"img/wiki/Xiao-removebg-preview-863746.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/SinisterbeadFusion-3eff00.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Zhangxiaofan_luxueqi_battle-f12e80.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Meetingbiyao_atnight-1e1d4f.png","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/Luxueqi_zhangxiaofan-cd7c8c.webp","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/桂莉_𝑮𝒖𝒊_𝑳𝒊_𝑆𝒉𝑎𝑛𝑔_𝑋𝑖𝑎𝑜𝑓𝑎𝑛-27bfc3.jpg","cap":""},{"src":"img/wiki/ZhangxiaofanS4-238599.webp","cap":"Season 4"}]},"Zhou Yixian":{"title":"Zhou Yixian","kind":"character","facts":{"species":["Human"],"gender":"Male"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Zhou Yixian is a key character in the novel Zhu Xian and its derivative works. He is male, over three hundred years old, and roams the jianghu as a fortune-teller and Taoist priest. His iconic image is that of holding a bamboo pole inscribed with the words “Immortal Points the Way.” He often makes a living by fortune-telling scams, yet he has a hidden connection to the lineage of Qingyunzi."},{"t":"h","x":"Appearance","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"His hair and beard are completely white, and his face carries an air of refined simplicity. He has a somewhat transcendent, crane-boned, immortal-like demeanor, resembling an enlightened master, which inspires a sense of respect at first glance. He carries a bamboo pole with a piece of white cloth attached, bearing the four characters: \"Immortal Points the Way\"."},{"t":"h","x":"Personality","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"His personality is humorous and open-minded; he is greedy, timid, yet fond of joining in the excitement. He is skilled in Qimen Dunjia arts such as Earth Evasion. Although he lives by deception, he is erudite and knowledgeable."},{"t":"h","x":"Background","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"Zhou Yixian appears throughout the book as a wise man who wanders the mundane world with a playful attitude. Beneath his seemingly common, streetwise words and actions lie unfathomable experience and cultivation. He serves as a crucial link connecting the righteous and evil factions and revealing hidden worldly affairs. The origins of his magical arts are closely related to the ancestral inheritance of the Qingyun Sect."},{"t":"h","x":"History","l":2},{"t":"p","x":"He is aware of the secret that Zhang Xiaofan bears the Four Volumes of the Heavenly Book, recognizes rare artifacts like the Qiankun Reincarnation Plate, and is called the “Encyclopedia of Jade Dynasty.” His interpersonal relationships are complex. He has frequent interactions with his granddaughter Zhou Xiaohuan and his son Zhou Xingyun, and also forms connections with both righteous and evil figures such as Zhang Xiaofan and Ghost King."}],"ep":27,"ch":null,"tags":[],"img":"img/wiki/Zou_Yixian_2-8ef277.png"},"Zhu Xian II (Novel)":{"title":"Zhu Xian II (Novel)","kind":"lore","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Zhu Xian II (诛仙第二部) is a sequel to the novel Zhu Xian by its original author, Xiao Ding. It was serialized on the Motie Chinese website in April 2012 and published in print in June of the same year. The story consists of four volumes and 124 chapters but was never completed; after a long hiatus, the publisher discontinued it."},{"t":"p","x":"The novel is set in the same universe as Zhu Xian but about ten years after the events of the first series. It focuses on a brand-new story with new characters. While it follows the story of Zhang Xiaofan after the original novel, he is only a side character; the main protagonist is a new character named Wang Zongjing (王宗景)."},{"t":"p","x":"There is some controversy regarding the authorship of Zhu Xian II. It is an original work published under the Motie Chinese Network and was written by one of their contracted authors. It is widely believed that Xiao Ding did not write the entirety of the sequel herself and instead used a ghostwriter. Her involvement was likely limited to initial concepts and oversight, providing early drafts, and allowing the use of her name for branding and marketing purposes."}],"img":"img/wiki/Zhu_Xian_II_novel-008538.webp"},"Zhu Xian Sword":{"title":"Zhu Xian Sword","kind":"item","facts":{},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The Zhu Xian Sword (诛仙剑, Immortal-Slaying Sword) is the most powerful divine artifact and the sacred treasure guarding the Qingyun Sect."},{"t":"p","x":"Born from the first ray of light in the universe, Pangu wielded the Zhuxian Sword to create the world, only to fall to the earth after exhausting his energy. The sword was discovered by Qingye, the founder of the Qingyun Sect, in the Huanyue Cave 1,300 years ago, and subsequently became the Qingyun Sect's signature sword. Possessing the power to slay gods and immortals, it also has a powerful bloodthirsty aura that can backfire on its wielder. As such, it must be wielded by someone who has reached the Taiqing Realm of the Taiji Xuanqing Dao and possesses a strong and steadfast mind. After Qingye revitalized the Qingyun Sect, he used the Zhuxian Sword to create the Zhuxian Sword Formation and sealed the spiritual energy of Qingyun's seven meridians with the Tianji Seal. Within the Huanyue Cave, the Zhuxian Sword's power increased tenfold."},{"t":"p","x":"Owners: Pangu → Qingye Zhenren → Tianchengzi → Daoxuan Zhenren → Zhang Xiaofan"}]}},"alias":{"Zhou Yi Xian":"Zhou Yixian","Heimu":"Hei Mu","Puzhi":"Master Puzhi","Youji":"You Ji","Gui Li":"Zhang Xiaofan","You Yi":"You Ji","Qinglong":"Qing Long","Beast God":"Beast Deity","Xiao Zhou":"Xiao Yicai","Deity Beast":"Beast Deity","Nian Da Lao":"Nian Lao Da","Qi Xiaoxian":"Qi Xiaoxuan","He Huan Sect":"HeHuan Sect","Heixin Laoren":"Black-Hearted Old Man","Qingye Daoist":"Daoist Qingye","Zeng Shuchang":"Zeng Shucang","Zheng Shucang":"Zeng Shucang","Heixin Lao Ren":"Black-Hearted Old Man","Tiang Yin Temple":"Tian Yin Temple","Burning Incense Valley":"Fen Xiang Valley"}};
